hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"9019","(9019) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Do not let Bilal’s call to prayer prevent you from your suhoor, for there is something in his sight. (Ahmad 3/1400 Abu Ali 2910)"
"9020","(9020) Abu Usama narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, he said: Sawad bin Hanzala al-Hilali narrated to us, on the authority of Samurah bin Jundub, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Bilal’s call to prayer, nor the long morning prayer, will not prevent you from suhoor. But the morning is rising on the horizon. (Tirmidhi 706. Ahmad 5/13)"
"9021","(9021) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: We had the suhoor meal with the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then we stood up for the prayer. We said: How much was there between them? He said: Reciting fifty verses. (Muslim 771, Tirmidhi 704)"
"9022","(9022) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Salem bin Ubaid Al Ashja’i, He said: I was with Abu Bakr, and he said: Get up and seek protection from me before dawn, then he ate."
"9023","(9023) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Shabib bin Gharqadiya, on the authority of Abu Aqeel, he said: I had the suhoor meal with Ali, then he ordered The muezzin is to perform the prayer."
"9024","(9024) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Jabala ibn Suhaim, on the authority of Aamir ibn Matar, who said: I came to Abd God is in His house, so He brought out for us the surplus of His suhoor, so we suhoored with him, and the prayer was established, so we went out and prayed with him."
"9025","(9025) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr, meaning Ibn Harith, who said: They were the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. People are quick to break their fast, and people are slow to do suhoor."
"9026","(9026) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ya’four, who said: I heard Abu Al-Sha’tha’i Jabir bin Zaid saying: They used to perform Suhoor. Now"
"9027","(9027) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Amr bin Marwan Abi Al-Anbas, who said: I heard Ibrahim say: It is from the Sunnah to delay Suhoor"
"9028","(9028) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Al-Walid bin Juma’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Tufayl narrated to us; He visited his family in Al-Jabbanah, then he came to Hudhayfah while he was in the house of Al-Harith bin Abi Rabi’ah. Then he found him, and he milked a camel for him, and he gave it to him, and he said: I want to fast, and he said: And I want to fast, so he drank his water, and took With his hand, he was led into the mosque when the prayer was performed."
"9029","(9029) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: It occurs between a man’s suhoor and The muezzin’s iqama is as long as he recites Surah Yusuf."
"9030","(9030) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymimi, on the authority of his father, he said: I went out with Hudhayf to Al-Mada'in in Ramadan, when dawn came, he said: Was any of you eating or drinking? We said: As for a man who wants to fast, no, then we walked until we slowed him down in prayer, then he came down and prayed."
"9031","(9031) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Among the morals of the prophets is delaying suhoor."
"9032","(9032) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He used to hasten part of his pre-dawn meal. To lead you to pray with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. This was conveyed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was sending Then he would eat with him until they all went out to pray together."
"9033","(9033) Affan told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Khubayb bin Abdul Rahman, he said: I heard your aunt say, and she was She performed Hajj with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: Ibn Umm is concealed. He calls for the night, so eat and drink until Bilal is called, and Bilal gives the call to prayer for the night, so eat and drink until the call is made. Ibn Umm Maktoum, she said: This one used to go up and this one came down, so we used to cling to him and say: As you are until we perform suhoor.\n(Tayalisi 1661. Tabarani 481)"
"9034","(9034) Abdou bin Sulaiman and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Asim bin Omar, on the authority of Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When the night comes from here, and the day departs from here, then The fasting person breaks his fast. (Abu Dawud 2343. Ahmad 1/28)"
"9035","(9035) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He greeted him while he was fasting on a journey, and when the sun had set, he said: O so-and-so, come down and work for us. He said: O Messenger of God, indeed upon you During the day, he said: Come down and treat us well. He said it three times, so he went down and did so, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, drank. Then he said: Then You have seen the night approaching here, and the fasting person has broken his fast.\n I said: And you are with him? He said: Yes. (Bukhari 1941. Muslim 773)"
"9036","(9036) Ziyad bin Al-Rabi’, who was trustworthy, narrated to us on the authority of Abu Jamra Al-Dhab’i; He used to break his fast with Ibn Abbas during Ramadan, and when he was gone in the evening, he would send his stepson to go up to the back of the house, and when she was gone The sun gives the call to prayer, so he eats and we eat. When he finishes, the prayer is performed, and he stands and prays, and we pray with him."
"9037","(9037) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Religion continues to prevail as long as people hasten breaking the fast. Indeed, the Jews and Christians delay it. (Abu Dawud 2345. Ahmad 2/450)"
"9038","(9038) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, that he heard him say: He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: People will continue to be well as long as they hasten their breaking of the fast, and do not delay it as their family did. The East (Bukhari 1957, Tirmidhi 699)"
"9039","(9039) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Omar used to write to his princes not to Be among those who procrastinate in breaking your fast, and do not wait with your prayers for the clash of stars."
"9040","(9040) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Tharwan ibn Malhan al-Taymi, who said: A man said to Ammar ibn Yasser: Abu Musa said: Do not break your fast when the stars appear, for that is the action of the Jews."
"9041","(9041) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: Abdullah was brought with his eyelids, and he said: To the people: Come closer and eat. Then one of them separated, and Abdullah said to him: What is the matter with you? He said: I am fasting, so Abdullah said: This is the one besides whom there is no god, when food is lawful for anyone to eat."
"9042","(9042) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: I entered upon him. So he broke his fast with a sweat, and I saw that the sun had not set."
"9043","(9043) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I would have brought Ibn Umar with his breakfast, and I would cover him."
"9044","(9044) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of al-Hijri, on the authority of a man from Banu Sawadhi, who said: I went to Hudhayfah, so I descended with him, and when the sun set, Hudhayfah and his companions descended. He did not stay but a short time until he broke his fast."
"9045","(۹۰۴۵) حَدَّثَنَا وَکِیعٌ ، عَنْ مُسْلِمِ بْنِ یَزِیدَ ، عَنْ أَبِیہِ ، قَالَ : کَانَ عَلِیُّ بْنُ أَبِی طَالِبٍ یَقُولُ لاِبْنِ Barker: Has the sun set? He says: Don't be in a hurry. He says: Has the sun set? He says: Don't be in a hurry. He says: Has the sun set? So if he said: Yes, he broke his fast, then he went down and prayed."
"9046","(9046) Omar bin Saad told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May the peace and blessings of God be upon him: This mother will remain well as long as they hasten to break the fast. (Muslim 771, Tirmidhi 699)"
"9047","(9047) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, who said: If you see that Asr has passed, so drink."
"9048","(9048) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas Amr bin Marwan, who said: I heard Ibrahim say: It is among the Sunnah to hasten. Breakfast"
"9049","(9049) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Musa bin Anas; Anas used to take the maidservant above the house and say: When the horizon is level, then inform me."
"9050","(9050) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Muwarriq Al-Ijlili, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, he said: Three of The morals of the prophets; Early in breaking the fast, early in suhoor, and placing the right over the left in prayer."
"9051","(9051) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of a statement, on the authority of Qays, who said: Omar gave a man a vessel next to him when the sun had set, and he said: To him: Drink, then he said: Perhaps you are one of those who procrastinate with his nature; I will, I will."
"9052","(9052) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Safwan bin Abdullah, on the authority of Umm Al-Darda’, on the authority of Ka’b bin Asim, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is not righteous to fast while traveling. (Ibn Majah 1644; Ahmad 434)"
"9053","(9053) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Saad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Al-Hasan, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on a journey, and he saw a man whom the people had gathered around, and he was shaded. Ali, and he said: What's wrong with him? They said: A fasting man, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is not righteous that you fast while travelling. (Bukhari 1946. Muslim 92)"
"9054","(9054) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Muwarriq, on the authority of Anas, who said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Travel. Among us is the fasting person and among us is the one who breaks the fast. Then those who break the fast rose up and beat the children and made the passengers drink. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he greeted: Those who broke the fast have gone today with the reward. (Muslim 788, Bayhaqi 243)"
"9055","(9055) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of His father, he said: The fasting person while traveling is like the one who breaks the fast while in the city."
"9056","(9056) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Jamra, who said: I asked Ibn Abbas about fasting while travelling? He said: Hardship and ease, take the ease of God for you."
"9057","(9057) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amer; He did not fast while travelling."
"9058","(9058) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Awf, he said: I heard that Al-Hasan used to say: Breaking the fast while traveling, and in the city. Your license"
"9059","(9059) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, that Ibn Abbas said: Breaking the fast in Traveling is my resolve."
"9060","(9060) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Breaking the fast while traveling is an act of charity towards God. May it be upon His servants."
"9061","(9061) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, fasted in the year of the conquest until he reached al-Kadaid, then he broke his fast. Rather, the last word is taken from the action of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Bukhari 2953, Ahmed 219)"
"9062","(9062) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, who said: I asked Abu Ja’ad about fasting while travelling? He said: Do not fast."
"9063","(9063) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Humaid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dhakwan; Ibn Omar stayed in Syria for two Ramadans and broke his fast."
"9064","(9064) Abu Khalid Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour bin Hayyan, who said: Saeed bin Jubayr said: Whoever accompanies me on a journey, do not He fasts"
"9065","(9065) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mudarris bin Abdullah, who said: I said to al-Sha`bi: I will perform the prayer at the point of prayer. He said: Pray two rak’ahs. I said: What about fasting? He said: Do not fast, break your fast even if you stay in prayer for ten years."
"9066","(9066) Abu Dawud Omar bin Saad told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on a journey, and Abu Bakr and Omar were with him, so he was brought food, and he said to them: Come closer and eat. They said: O Messenger of God, we are fasting. He said: Go to your companion. Work for your companion. Come closer. So both. (Nasa’i 2572. Ahmad 2/336)"
"9067","(9067) Abu Muawiyah and Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: Anas was asked about fasting while travelling? He said: Whoever breaks his fast will be relieved, and whoever fasts, fasting is better."
"9068","(9068) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulki, who said: I accompanied Aisha on the travel, so what She broke her fast until she entered Mecca."
"9069","(9069) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of al-Hakam ibn Atiyya, on the authority of al-Nadr ibn Abdullah al-Qaisi, on the authority of Qais Ibn Abbad; He used to fast while traveling and break his fast."
"9070","(9070) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Musa Mawla Ibn Amir, who said: I asked Anas about fasting while travelling? He said: We were with Abu Musa on a journey, and he fasted and we fasted."
"9071","(9071) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Al-Aswad; That his father used to fast while travelling."
"9072","(9072) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad used to fast while travelling."
"9073","(9073) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: I saw Aisha fasting while traveling: until he made her suffer. Toxins"
"9074","(9074) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas used to say about This is like the saying of Anas bin Malik."
"9075","(9075) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to go out into the forest and would not break his fast or shorten his prayers."
"9076","(9076) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas said: Fasting while traveling is better. And breaking the fast is a concession."
"9077","(9077) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Khams, who said: Salem was asked, or I was asked about fasting while travelling? He said: If you fast, then it will be sufficient for you, and if you break your fast, then it will be permitted for you."
"9078","(9078) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha; That Hamza Al-Aslami asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about fasting while travelling?"
"9079","(9079) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of the common people, he said: I said to Mujahid: Which of these do you like most? He said: If you are able to fast, then fasting is more amazing to me."
"9080","(9080) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ash’ath ibn Abi al-Sha’tha’i, who said: I accompanied my father and Amr ibn Maymun. Al-Aswad bin Yazid and Abu Wael used to fast Ramadan and other days while traveling."
"9081","(9081) Ubaidah bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, he said: Hudhayfah asked permission to go to Al-Mada'in, and Hudhayfah said to me: On the condition that she does not shorten her hair and does not break her fast."
"9082","(9082) Muhammad bin Bishr Al-Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: We went out with the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Mecca to Hunayn, on the twelve remaining days of Ramadan, and he fasted. A group of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and others broke the fast, so he did not care about that. (Muslim 94. Ahmad 3/92)"
"9083","(9083) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiyyah, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: We used to fight with The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Among us is the fasting person and some of us is the one who breaks the fast.” The fasting person does not blame the one who breaks the fast, nor does the one who breaks the fast blame the fasting person."
"9084","(9084) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, he said: I went out and was silent, and they said to me: Repeat. He said: I said: Indeed, Anas They told me that the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were traveling, so the fasting person should not blame the one who breaks his fast, nor should The one who breaks the fast is on the fasting person. I met Ibn Abi Malika and he told me something similar on the authority of Aisha."
"9085","(9085) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, Al-Hasan, and Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab. They said: They were the companions of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. They travel, and the one who fasts fasts, and the one who breaks the fast breaks his fast. The fasting person does not blame the one who breaks the fast, nor does the one who breaks the fast blame the one who breaks the fast. The fasting person"
"9086","(9086) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s peace and blessings be upon him. Among us is the fasting person and among us is the one who breaks the fast. He did not find fault with one of us over the other."
"9087","(9087) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: We were with Abdullah’s companions on a journey, and some of them fasted. And some of them broke the fast."
"9088","(9088) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Imran al-Qattan, on the authority of Ammar, the client of Banu Hashim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He was asked about a man who fasted Ramadan while travelling? He said: It is not sufficient."
"9089","(9089) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Al-Muharrir bin Abi Hurairah, he said: I fasted Ramadan while travelling, so Abu Hurairah ordered me to repeat fasting among my family."
"9090","(9090) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Al-Fayd, who said: We were on a campaign, and an emir was against us, and he said: No. You shall fast, so whoever fasts let him break his fast. Abu al-Fayd said: I met Abu Qursafa, a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I asked him about that? He said: If I had fasted and then fasted, I would not have done so."
"9091","(9091) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of a man, on the authority of his father; A man fasted Ramadan while travelling, so Omar, may God have mercy on him, ordered him to celebrate Eid."
"9092","(9092) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaydah, he said: I asked him about God Almighty says: {So whoever of you witnesses the month, let him fast during it}? He said: Whoever witnesses the beginning of it, let him fast the end of it. Do you not see what God Almighty says: {So whoever of you witnesses the month, let him fast}."
"9093","(9093) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: If the month of Ramadan begins, it does not end. If he refuses to leave, let him complete his fast."
"9094","(9094) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ali, may God Almighty have mercy on him, who said: When Ramadan approaches you and it is... A resident then travels, let him fast."
"9095","(9095) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, Amr ibn Murrā narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Al-Bakhtari narrating, on the authority of Ubaidah, that he said about a man who fasts for a few days of Ramadan, then leaves. He said: He fasts. Ibn Abbas said: If he wishes, he may fast, and if he wishes, he may break his fast."
"9096","(9096) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He went out during Ramadan and broke his fast."
"9097","(9097) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said: There is no harm in traveling during Ramadan, and it breaks the fast if I wish"
"9098","(9098) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, fasted in the year of the conquest until he reached al-Kadid, then he broke his fast."
"9099","(9099) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I asked my servants: Should I travel during Ramadan? He said: No."
"9100","(9100) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein; He was asked about a people who traveled during Ramadan? He said: They fast."
"9101","(9101) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah; In the words of God Almighty: {And upon those who are able to endure it is a ransom, feeding the poor.} He said: It is abrogated. {So whoever of you witnesses the month Let him fast}"
"9102","(9102) Abdul Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: This has been abrogated. The verse: {So whoever of you witnesses the month, let him fast} the verse that comes after it."
"9103","(9103) Abdul Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Yazid, on the authority of Umm Dharhi, who said: I came to Aisha, and she said: Where did you come from? So I said: From my brother, and she said: What is the matter with him? I said: I bid him farewell. He wants to leave. She said: So extend my greetings to him, and pass by him and let him stand. If he catches up with me while I am on the other side of the road, I will stand, meaning Ramadan."
"9104","(9104) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: Abu Misra set out on a journey during Ramadan, and he passed by the Euphrates while he was fasting, so he took He tasted some of it, drank it and broke his fast."
"9105","(9105) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and Al-Hasan. They said: He breaks the fast if he wants."
"9106","(9106) Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ismail Ibn Aliya narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ward bin Thamamah, on the authority of Al-Lajlaj, he said: We were traveling with Omar, may God be pleased with him, for three miles, and he would stop praying and break his fast."
"9107","(9107) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, who said: I asked Sa`id bin al-Musayyab: Should I shorten the prayer? Should I break my fast in Ramadan? He said: Yes, and he is far away from Medina."
"9108","(9108) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ said: Fasting while traveling is like prayer, it is shortened when She broke her fast, and fasts if she completes the prayer."
"9109","(9109) Omar bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, who said: I asked Al-Zuhri: How long should the prayer be shortened? He said: In careful travel. He said: I said: What is carefulness in yourself? He said: Two days."
"9110","(9110) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymimi, on the authority of his father, who said: I was with Hudhayfah. In Al-Mada'in, he said: I asked him for permission to return to my family, and he said: I do not give you permission unless you resolve not to break the fast until you enter. He said: That was during Ramadan. I said: I resolve to myself that I will not break my fast, nor shorten my fast until I go to my family."
"9111","(9111) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Marthad; Abu Misra traveled during Ramadan and broke his fast at the bridge gate."
"9112","(9112) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Do not fast before Ramadan. Fast when you see it and break your fast when you see it. If something prevents you from seeing it, then continue. Thirty (Tirmidhi 688 and Abu Ali 2355)"
"9113","(9113) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ruba’i, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not advance the month unless you see the crescent, or complete the number of days, and do not break your fast until You will see the crescent, or complete the counting. (Abu Dawud 2320. An-Nasa’i 2436)"
"9114","(9114) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Fast to see it. And break your fast when you see it, and if it is cloudy over you, then complete thirty."
"9115","(9115) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Do not pray Ramadan with anything, and do not come forward. One day before, not two days."
"9116","(9116) Abu Asama told us, Ubaid Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned Ramadan and said: Fast when you see it and break your fast when you see it. If he faints, upon you, so appreciate it. (Muslim 5. Ahmad 2/13)"
"9117","(9117) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned the crescent, and he said: When you see it, fast, and when you see it, break your fast. If you faint, then count thirty. (Muslim 20. Abu Ali 6252)"
"9118","(9118) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: It is forbidden to It is hastened a day or two before Ramadan."
"9119","(9119) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Al-Ala bin Abdul Rahman bin Yaqoub, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Huraira, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If it is the middle of Sha`ban, then hold off until the end of Sha`ban. Ramadan. (Tirmidhi 738 and Abu Dawud 2330)"
"9120","(9120) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, who said: We went out for Umrah. When we camped in the valley of palm trees, he said: We saw the crescent. Some of the people said: He is the son of three years old, and some of the people said: He is Ibn Laylatan, so we met Ibn Abbas and said: Indeed, we saw the crescent. Some of the people said: He is the son of three, and some said: The people: He is the son of two nights. He said: On what night did you see him? He said: So we said: For such-and-such night, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: God has extended a period of vision. So, for the night you have seen it. (Muslim 29. Tabarani 12487)"
"9121","(9121) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murr, who said: I heard Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: Have we made Ramadan halal? We were in Dhath Irq, so we sent a man to Ibn Abbas to ask him? Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God has given him time to see it, so if you faint So they completed the count. (Muslim 30 Ahmad 1/327)"
"9122","(9122) Hushaym told us, he said: Mujalid told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali; When Ramadan came, he would deliver a sermon and say: Do not go ahead of the month. When you see the crescent, fast, and when you see the crescent, fast. The crescent moon, then break your fast. If you faint, then complete the count. He said: He used to say that after the afternoon prayer, and after Fajr prayer."
"9123","(9123) Hushaym told us, Mujalid told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Omar, similar to that."
"9124","(9124) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad. They said: It was forbidden to come before Ramadan. By fasting."
"9125","(9125) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, and Ata’; They both disliked hastening before Ramadan."
"9126","(9126) Jarir told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning a man who fasts and attends Ramadan, he said: There are days between him and Ramadan."
"9127","(9127) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Qalaab, who said: They used to look at the crescent, and if They saw it, they fasted, and if they did not see it, they looked at what their imam said."
"9128","(9128) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Umm Salama; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to connect Sha`ban with Ramadan. (Tirmidhi 736. Ahmad 6/300)"
"9129","(9129) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not precede Ramadan by fasting a day, or two days, except for a man. If he used to fast, let him fast. (Muslim 21. Tirmidhi 685)"
"9130","(9130) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If a man is fasting regularly, there is no harm in him praying."
"9131","(9131) Ismail bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun; That Muhammad prepared the suhoor while thinking that night was upon him, then it became clear to him that he had suhoor after the morning, so he said: As for me Today is breaking the fast."
"9132","(9132) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; Whoever eats suhoor while thinking that it is night, then it becomes clear that he did suhoor and dawn has come? Let him complete his fast."
"9133","(9133) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked the ruling about a man who uses Suhoor while he thinks that he is obligated to do so. At night? He said: He completes his fast."
"9134","(9134) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, who said: If he eats after dawn has come He has completed his fast, and made up for the day in its place."
"9135","(9135) Sa’l bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who had suhoor and thought that night was upon him, he said: He will complete his fast."
"9136","(9136) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr ibn Haram, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: He completes his fast."
"9137","(9137) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Abdullah said: Whoever eats at the beginning of the day, let him eat. The last one"
"9138","(9138) Ali bin Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Jabalah bin Suhaim, on the authority of Ali bin Hanzali, on the authority of his father He said: I saw Omar bin Al-Khattab in Ramadan, and a drink was offered to him, and some of the people drank while they saw that the sun had set. Then the muezzin rose and said: O Commander of the Faithful, by God, the sun is rising and has not set, so Omar said: May God protect us from your polytheism. Two times, or three times, oh, whoever breaks his fast should fast one day in place of another day, and whoever does not If he breaks his fast, let him complete it until the sun sets."
"9139","(9139) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabalah ibn Suhaym, on the authority of Ali ibn Hanzali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar, The like, except that Sufyan said: We did not send you as a shepherd, but rather we sent you as a caller, and we have striven hard and made up for the day. It is easy."
"9140","(9140) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Alaqi, on the authority of someone who heard Bishr ibn Qays; Omar, may God have mercy on him, ordered them to judge."
"9141","(9141) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Fatima bint Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Asmaa; They broke their fast at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a cloudy day, and then the sun rose.\n Abu Asama said: So I said to Hisham: So they were ordered to judge? He said: Is that bad? (Abu Dawud 2351. Ahmad 6/346)"
"9142","(9142) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He will judge, because God Almighty says: {Complete the fast until nightfall}"
"9143","(9143) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, Mansour bin Abi Al-Aswad narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahhab, on the authority of Omar, based on the following hadith of Abu Muawiyah."
"9144","(9144) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: Al-Hasan used to say about someone who broke his fast when he saw that the sun had set, Then it became clear to him that she had not disappeared. He said: He was saying: It is sufficient."
"9145","(9145) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: Asas was expelled from the house of Hafsiya and Ali. The sky was clouds, so they thought that the sun had set, so they broke their fast. It was not long before the clouds cleared, and suddenly the sun was rising. Omar said: What? We differed from sin."
"9146","(9146) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Qatan, on the authority of his father, he said: He was with Mu’awiyah. In Ramadan, they broke their fast, then the sun rose, so he ordered them to make up for it."
"9147","(9147) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I said: I broke my fast on a cloudy day in the month of Ramadan. Ramadan, and I thought it was the night, then the sun rose. Should I ever make up that day and not make amends? He said: Yes."
"9148","(9148) Abu Asama narrated to us, Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I invaded the land of the Romans with Ziyad bin Al-Nadr, he said: So We made Ramadan an end, and the people fasted, and among them were the companions of Abdullah. Amer bin Saad, Sami’, Abu Abdullah, Abu Muammar, and Abu Musafa’, so the people broke their fast one day while the sky was cloudy. We are between two mountains; Al-Harith and Al-Huwarith, and I did not break my fast until night began. Then the sun came out and we saw it on the mountain. Ziyad said: But This day we will make up for it, and we did not intend to break it."
"9149","(9149) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of his father; Omar broke his fast during the month of Ramadan, and it was said to him: The sun has risen, and he said: That is all right, we were both struggling."
"9150","(9150) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, who said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and asked him about suhoor? A man who was sitting with him said to him: Eat until you do not doubt. So Ibn Abbas said to him: This man does not say anything, eat as long as you doubt. So that you do not doubt"
"9151","(9151) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Walid, he said: Aoun bin Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Two men entered upon Ali. Abu Bakr was eating suhoor, and one of them said: Fajr has come, and the other said: It has not yet risen. Abu Bakr said: Everything has come. They disagreed."
"9152","(9152) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Walid, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Bakr, something like this."
"9153","(9153) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Amara bin Zazan, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: I saw Ibn Umar taking a bucket of Zamzam, and he said: To two men: Has dawn come? One of them said: No, and the other said: Yes, so he drank."
"9154","(9154) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Aqmar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Eat until you see an objection."
"9155","(9155) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Eat until you see it like the slit of a tongue."
"9156","(9156) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ata`, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said to two of his boys, while he was in Umm’s house. He was in the month of Ramadan while he was eating his suhoor meal, and one of them said: Fajr has come, and the other said: It has not come. He said: Isqianiya."
"9157","(9157) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: Eat until the dawn becomes clear to you."
"9158","(9158) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid bin Zaid, who said: I heard Al-Hasan and a man said to him: Should I perform Suhoor? What do you want to do in the morning? He said: Whatever you decide, by God, nothing is hidden in the morning."
"9159","(9159) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Fadl ibn Dulham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Umar said: If two men doubt about dawn, Let them eat until we wake up."
"9160","(9160) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim bin Subaih, who said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and said: When should I give up suhoor? A man sitting with him said: Eat until you are in doubt, so leave it. He said: Eat whenever you are in doubt until you no longer doubt."
"9161","(9161) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad said: I placed the vessel on my hands and began to see whether dawn had come?"
"9162","(9162) Mulazim bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Numan, on the authority of Qays bin Talq, he said: Abu Talq bin Ali narrated to us, The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Eat and drink, and do not let the shining light that ascends intimidate you. Eat and drink until Red objected to you and said thus with his hand. (Tirmidhi 7050 Abu Dawud 2340)"
"9163","(9163) Abu Usama narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, he said: Sawad bin Hanzala Al-Hilali narrated to us, on the authority of Samurah bin Jundub, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Bilal’s call to prayer will not prevent you from suhoor, nor will the long morning prayer. But the morning is rising on the horizon."
"9164","(9164) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of his maternal uncle, on the authority of Thawban, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: The dawn is two dawns. As for the one who is as if it were the tail of the wanderer, he does not make anything lawful, nor does he make it unlawful, but he is the one who is arrogant. (Dar Qatni 2. Bayhaqi 215)"
"9165","(9165) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit ibn Amara, on the authority of Ghunaim ibn Qays, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: It is not the dawn that Thus, it means the rectangle, but the dawn that is like this, means the interceptor."
"9166","(9166) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hawshab bin Aqeel, on the authority of Ja`far bin Nahar, who said: I asked al-Qasim: Is it the shining one, or the intercepting one? He said: The one who opposes, and the one who shines: the false morning."
"9167","(9167) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: The bright one is the false morning, but if Morning broke on the horizon."
"9168","(9168) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, who said: They were not counting dawn because of this, but it was They were counting the dawn that would fill the homes and roads."
"9169","(9169) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Adiy bin Thabit, who said: We disagreed at dawn, so we came. Ibrahim, and he said: The dawn is two dawns. As for one of them, the bright dawn does not make prayer permissible and does not make food forbidden, and as for the passing, red dawn, it makes prayer permissible. Food and drink are forbidden."
"9170","(9170) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir and Ata’, who said: The intervening dawn that is beside it. Red"
"9171","(9171) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: I asked Al-Zuhri and Maymun, and I said: I want to fast. So I see the bright pillar of morning? So they said together: Eat and drink until you see it across the horizon of the heavens."
"9172","(9172) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Adiy ibn Hatim, who said: When it was revealed: “Until it becomes clear The white thread is more distinct than the black thread.} He said: Udayy said: O Messenger of God, I will put two sashes under my pillow; A black headband and a white headband, so I can tell night from day. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Your pillow is long. Broad, it is the blackness of the night and the whiteness of the day. (Bukhari 1916 and Abu Dawud 2341)"
"9173","(9173) Mu’tamir bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The fasting person has the choice, what is between him? And in the middle of the day."
"9174","(9174) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The fasting person With the option between it and midday."
"9175","(9175) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: Whoever tells himself to fast has made the choice. Unless he speaks until the day extends."
"9176","(9176) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: If you wake up in the morning and you want to fast You have the choice: if you wish, you may fast, and if you wish, you may break your fast, unless you force yourself to fast during the night."
"9177","(9177) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, who said: Abdullah said: I am one of you with one of the two views. Unless he eats or drinks."
"9178","(9178) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I said to Abraham: The man in voluntary fasting has a choice between him and Midday? He said: Yes."
"9179","(9179) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The fasting person has the choice between him and the middle of the day, so if If he exceeds that, he will only have it as much as the rest of the day."
"9180","(9180) Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, about fasting. He has the choice as long as he is not fasting in the morning, then if he is fasting in the morning he will fast."
"9181","(9181) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of Saad ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: A man has no choice. He does not eat until midday, so if it seems to him that he should eat something, and if it seems to him that he should make it a fast, then he is fasting."
"9182","(9182) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; What about a man who wants to fast? He said: He has the option until midnight."
"9183","(9183) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man does Suhoor, then he is obliged to fast. If he breaks the fast, he has to make it up, and if he intends to fast, then he has the choice. If he wants, he may fast, and if he wants, he may break the fast, and if someone asks him, He said: Are you fasting? He said: Yes, it is obligatory for him to fast unless he says, “If God wills,” and if he says, then he has the option. If he wants, he may fast, and if he wants, he may fast. He broke his fast."
"9184","(9184) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abi Abdul Rahman; That his dream appeared to him during fasting after the sun had set, so he fasted."
"9185","(9185) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; Aisha and Hafsa were fasting in the morning and broke their fast, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to make up for it."
"9186","(9186) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Uthman Al-Batti, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin; He fasted on the day of his death and was extremely thirsty, so he broke his fast. So he asked a number of the Prophet’s companions, may God bless him and grant him peace? So they ordered him to spend a day in his place."
"9187","(9187) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: He spends a day His place"
"9188","(9188) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, who said: I asked an alcoholic person about a man who had become fasting in the morning. Did his mother tell him to break the fast? He said: It is as if he hated that, and he said: He will spend a day in his place."
"9189","(9189) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man eats suhoor, he is obligated to fast. He broke his fast, so he has to make up for it."
"9190","(9190) Abdul Rahim bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, on the authority of Ata’ and Mujahid; If they visited a man and were invited to eat while they were fasting, if he asked them to break his fast, they would break his fast. They say: We complete a day in its place."
"9191","(9191) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ibn Umm Hani’, on the authority of Umm Hani’, who said: I was sitting with the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, brought him a drink and he drank from it, then he handed it to me and she drank. She said: So I said: O Messenger of God, I have sinned, so ask forgiveness for me. He said: What is that? She said: I was fasting and broke my fast. He said: Is there a fulfillment you were fulfilling? She said: No, he said: It will not harm you. (Tirmidhi 731, Ahmad 6/343)"
"9192","(9192) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Ibn Abbas used to break the fast of voluntary fasts, and he did not He cares."
"9193","(9193) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Yusuf ibn Mahak al-Makki, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He had intercourse with his neighbor while he was fasting. He said: So it was said to him: Did you have intercourse with her while you were fasting? He said: My maid liked me, but it was voluntary."
"9194","(9194) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, who said: He did not see any harm in a man fasting in the morning, then He breaks his fast."
"9195","(9195) Ibn Fadil told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Perhaps I was guided. We have the opposite, so we say: Were it not for your fasting, we would bring her closer to you, so he supplicates for her and we break her fast."
"9196","(9196) Ubaidah told us, on the authority of Abu Miskin, he said: Ibrahim and Sa`id bin Jubayr were in a lawsuit, and he said Saeed: I had told myself to fast, then I would eat. Ibrahim said: I do not like you."
"9197","(9197) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of a statement, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he wakes up in the morning while he is fasting, he does not break his fast."
"9198","(9198) Ibn Fadil told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Perhaps the Messenger of God called May God’s prayers and peace be upon him when he had his lunch, but he did not find it, so he was required to fast that day."
"9199","(9199) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Umm al-Darda’, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’; Perhaps he called for lunch and did not find it, so fasting is required of him on that day."
"9200","(9200) Al-Thaqafi told us, and Yazid, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas; That Abu Talha used to come to his family and say: Do you have any lunch? If they say no, he says: Then I am fasting. Al-Thaqafi added: If he had them, he would break his fast."
"9201","(9201) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Muadh; He used to come to his family after noon and say: Do you have lunch? So they would apologize to him, and he would say: I am fasting for the rest of my day. Then they would say to him: You will fast at the end of the day! He says: Whoever does not fast the last part of it, will not fast the first part of it."
"9202","(9202) Abd al-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Umm al-Darda’, she said: Abu al-Darda’ used to go out in the morning. Sometimes, he comes and asks for lunch, and perhaps he does not agree with us, so he says: Then I am fasting."
"9203","(9203) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qahdham, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, he said: Muadh used to come After he sacrifices his family, he will ask them and say: Do you have anything? If they say no, he fasts that day."
"9204","(9204) Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Hazim, he said: Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm told me On the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Hafsa, who said, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no fasting for one who does not practice it. At night (Tirmidhi 730, Abu Dawud 2446)"
"9205","(9205) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Hafsa, that she said: There is no fasting for those who do not complete the fast before dawn."
"9206","(9206) Yahya bin Sulaym al-Taifi told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Muhammad bin al-Munkadir, he said: I was informed that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about cutting off the missed days of Ramadan? He said: That is yours, so he said: Have you seen that if one of you was in debt and he paid off a dirham and two dirhams, would you not have paid it? ? And God has more right to pardon and forgive. (Daraqutni 77)"
"9207","(9207) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, and Abu Hurairah, who said: There is no harm in making up for Ramadan is divided."
"9208","(9208) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Bakr informed me, on the authority of Anas, he said: If you wish, complete Ramadan. Successively, or separately, if you wish."
"9209","(9209) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair; Concerning making up for the days of Ramadan, he said: If he wishes, he may choose."
"9210","(9210) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, that he said regarding making up for the missed days of Ramadan He said: Count the waiting period and fast however you wish."
"9211","(9211) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Salih, on the authority of Musa ibn Yazid ibn Muhabab, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Malik bin Yakhamir, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal; He was asked about making up for Ramadan? He said: Count the waiting period, and fast as you wish."
"9212","(9212) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Rafi’ bin Khadij, on the authority of his grandmother, that Rafi’ He used to say: Count the waiting period and fast as you wish."
"9213","(9213) Muammar bin Sulaiman Al-Ruqi told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A woman came to Ibn Abbas to ask him about Making up for Ramadan fasts? He said: Count the numbers and divide them. He said: Sa`id bin Jubayr and Ikrimah used to say that."
"9214","(9214) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Mujahid, Tawus, and Sa’id bin Jubayr. They said: If you wish. Spend Ramadan consecutively or separately."
"9215","(9215) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, Ata’, Mujahid, and Tawus; Because they saw no harm in separating the missed days of Ramadan."
"9216","(9216) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Mujahid; Concerning a man who is obligated to fast from Ramadan, so he breaks his fast, or he continues it. He said: Indeed, God intends ease for His servants. Let him see if that is easiest for him. If he wants, he can join him, and if he wants, he can separate."
"9217","(9217) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Zuhayr, one of Abu Misra’s companions. ; Abu Misra used to stop making up for Ramadan."
"9218","(9218) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: If it is difficult for you to make up for it consecutively, separate. It is only a number of other days."
"9219","(9219) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah; {Then a number of other days}. He said: If He wills, He will join, and if He wills, He will separate."
"9220","(9220) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyya told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: He did not see To complete Ramadan intermittently."
"9221","(9221) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; Concerning making up for Ramadan, if you wish, it may be consecutive, or it may be separate if you wish."
"9222","(9222) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Maimun, who said: Making up for Ramadan is more frequent than other days."
"9223","(9223) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail al-Makki, on the authority of Rabi’i, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, who said: There is no harm in separation. Make up for Ramadan."
"9224","(9224) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; With regard to making up for the missed days of Ramadan, fast as you wish, and Ibn Umar said: Fast as you broke your fast."
"9225","(9225) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Mu’awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, Azhar ibn Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Amer. Al-Wazani said: I heard Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah, and he was asked about making up days of Ramadan separately? He said: Count the waiting period, and fast as you wish."
"9226","(9226) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said regarding making up the days of Ramadan: He should follow it up."
"9227","(9227) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He was commanded to make up for Ramadan consecutively."
"9228","(9228) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Whoever is obligated to fast during Ramadan, Let him fast continuously, and not separate them."
"9229","(9229) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: He frequently makes up for the days of Ramadan."
"9230","(9230) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, that he said: He does not sever it if it is authentic."
"9231","(9231) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to say: Make up the days of Ramadan one by one."
"9232","(9232) Abdo told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The case is like a body."
"9233","(9233) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Al-Hasan loved to follow the days of Ramadan."
"9234","(9234) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: I would prefer that he make up for it the way he broke his fast."
"9235","(9235) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said regarding making up for the missed days of Ramadan: He is most beloved to me if he fasts. Just as he broke his fast."
"9236","(9236) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, on the authority of Uqba ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: He can perform it if he wishes."
"9237","(9237) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam. He said: I asked him about making up for the missed days of Ramadan? He said: Consecutive is more beloved to me."
"9238","(9238) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of al-Qasim, who said: Fast it consecutively unless he interrupts you as he interrupted you. Therein"
"9239","(9239) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulaiman, on the authority of Ata’, he said: He makes his case consecutively. He is dearer to me, even if he separates his parts."
"9240","(9240) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of God May the peace and blessings of God be upon him and his family while fasting. (Abu Dawud 2356, Darqutni 2)"
"9241","(9241) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He did not see any harm in using the siwak for a fasting person."
"9242","(9242) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, and Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Nahik, on the authority of Ziyad bin Hudayr, who said: What I saw someone using a siwak while fasting from Omar bin Al-Khattab."
"9243","(9243) Ubaidah bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Abu Nayyak, on the authority of Ziyad bin Hudayr, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him. May God bless him, in the same way."
"9244","(9244) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shaddad Abi Talhah, on the authority of a woman among them who was called a ram. She said: I came to Aisha asked about the siwak for the fasting person? She said: This is your siwak in my hand and I am fasting."
"9245","(9245) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Jalil, he said: Shahr bin Hawshab narrated to me, he said: Ibn Abbas was asked About the siwak for the fasting person? He said: What a beautiful purity, stay calm under all circumstances."
"9246","(9246) Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; He used to eat food twice, in the morning and in the evening, and he was fasting."
"9247","(9247) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Rest at the beginning of the day, and do not rest at the end of the day if you are Fasting, I said: Why don't I take a nap at the end of the day? He said: The breath of a fasting person is sweeter to God than the scent of musk."
"9248","(9248) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Muhammad used to stay in peace at the beginning of the day, and he hated it at the end of it."
"9249","(9249) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to fast when he wanted to go to noon and he was fasting."
"9250","(9250) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in using the siwak for the fasting person."
"9251","(9251) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Sha’bi, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Salim; He saw no harm in using the siwak for a fasting person, except when the sun was turning yellow."
"9252","(9252) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; It is disliked for a fasting person to use the siwak after noon."
"9253","(9253) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: The fasting person may stay in peace any day he wishes."
"9254","(9254) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Bashir, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he was asked about the siwak. To the fasting person, and he said: I bleed my mouth twice today."
"9255","(9255) Ibn Abi Ghaniyy told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam; He saw no harm in using the siwak for one who was fasting at the beginning of the day, and he said: It was only disliked for him at the end of the day, after he had left his mouth. It is desirable for him to return to his stomach."
"9256","(9256) Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, who said: Saeed bin Al-Musayyab was asked about the siwak for a fasting person? He said: There is no harm in it."
"9257","(9257) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father; He used to use a wet siwak while fasting."
"9258","(9258) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no harm in the wet siwak for the fasting person."
"9259","(9259) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no harm in the wet siwak for the fasting person."
"9260","(9260) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He saw no harm in using the wet siwak while he was fasting."
"9261","(9261) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in the wet siwak for the fasting person."
"9262","(9262) Ubaid bin Sahil Al-Ghadani told us, on the authority of Uqba bin Abi Jasra Al-Mazini, who said: A man came to Ibn Sirin. He said: What do you think of the siwak for a fasting person? He said: There is no problem with it. He said: It is fresh and has a taste. He said: And water has a taste and you rinse your mouth."
"9263","(9263) Zayd ibn al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim? He said: There is no harm in him using a fresh oud while fasting."
"9264","(9264) Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq told us, Abu Hamza told us, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Sayegh, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar. He said: There is no harm in a fasting person using the wet or dry siwak."
"9265","(9265) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Salama, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; He hated it and said: It is sweet and bitter."
"9266","(9266) Abd al-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha’, on the authority of al-Hakam; He disliked the wet siwak for the fasting person."
"9267","(9267) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Misra; He disliked the wet siwak for the fasting person."
"9268","(9268) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If it is dry, then it gets wet."
"9269","(9269) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He will remain in peace, and he will not get wet."
"9270","(9270) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; It is permissible for a fasting person to chew gum as long as it does not enter his throat."
"9271","(9271) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is no harm in chewing gum for a fasting person as long as he does not swallow it. His saliva"
"9272","(9272) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Aisha saw no harm in chewing. Chewing gum is for the fasting person, except for bitumen, and it was permitted for bitumen only."
"9273","(9273) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm for a fasting person to chew gum. And he does not swallow his saliva."
"9274","(9274) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; It is disliked for the fasting person."
"9275","(9275) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Issa, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; It is disliked for a fasting person to chew gum."
"9276","(9276) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; He hated it, and said: It is marwa."
"9277","(9277) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Malik, a man from the people of the Levant, on the authority of a man who named him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his mother His beloved, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; She disliked chewing gum for a fasting person."
"9278","(9278) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: If vomiting overtakes him, it is not He has to make up for it, and if he draws water, then he has to make up for it."
"9279","(9279) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to say: Whoever is overcome by vomiting while fasting does not break his fast, and whoever vomits has broken his fast."
"9280","(9280) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If a fasting person vomits, he should repeat it. (Abu Dawud 2372. Ahmad 2/498)"
"9281","(9281) Azhar Al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin, who said: If a fasting person starts vomiting, he does not break his fast. And if he vomits, he breaks his fast."
"9282","(9282) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a fasting person who vomits, he said: If it was vomiting, then he must make up for it, and if it was vomiting, then he does not have to make it up."
"9283","(9283) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When vomiting overtakes him, then do not repeat it. And if he hesitates, he must repeat it."
"9284","(9284) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Habban al-Salami, on the authority of al-Qasim bin Muhammad, he said: The fasting person If he is overcome by vomiting, he does not have to make up for it, but if he vomits intentionally, he does not have to make up for it."
"9285","(9285) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Qays, who said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about the man who precedes him. He vomited while fasting, should he make up for that day? He said: No."
"9286","(9286) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amer; If he vomits intentionally, he has broken his fast."
"9287","(9287) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If The fasting person vomits and has broken his fast."
"9288","(9288) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: If a man vomits while he is fasting He is obligated to make up for it, but if he is overcome by vomiting, then he is not obligated to make up for it."
"9289","(9289) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: If a fasting person vomits He intentionally broke his fast, and if vomiting overtook him, there is nothing wrong with him."
"9290","(9290) Abdul Rahim bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, similar to him."
"9291","(9291) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu al-Jawdi, on the authority of Balj al-Mahri, on the authority of Abu Shaybah Al-Mahri said: It was said to Thawban: Tell us on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I saw the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he vomited and broke his fast. (Ahmad 283. Tahawi 96)"
"9292","(9292) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ya’ish. Ibn Al-Walid Ibn Hisham, that Ma’dan informed him, that Abu Al-Darda’ informed him; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, vomited and broke his fast. He said: Then I found two garments, and he said: I poured water for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he blessed his ablution. (Tirmidhi 87. Abu Dawud 2373)"
"9293","(9293) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Breaking the fast is with what comes in, not what comes out."
"9294","(9294) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, who said: Amer was asked about a fasting person vomiting? He said: If he suddenly vomits, he does not make up for it, but if he vomited intentionally, then he has broken his fast."
"9295","(9295) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, who said: Abu Huraira said: If the fasting person breaks his fast So he rinsed his mouth, not rinsing his mouth, but covering his mouth."
"9296","(9296) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: Did I ask Abraham about that? He said: There is no harm in him being glorified."
"9297","(9297) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: It will continue This nation will be fine as long as they hasten to break the fast. If it is the day of one of you’s fast and he rinses his rinse mouth, there is no right for him, but To drink it, for the best of it is the first one."
"9298","(9298) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; He hated to rinse his mouth when breaking his fast."
"9299","(9299) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: There is no harm in rinsing the mouth when breaking the fast."
"9300","(9300) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He disliked it for a man to rinse his mouth when he broke his fast, or if he wanted to drink."
"9301","(9301) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam; He was asked about a fasting person rinsing his mouth? He thought that"
"9302","(9302) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; It is disliked for the fasting person to rinse his mouth."
"9303","(9303) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Othman, who said: I saw Ibn Omar while he was fasting, urinating The garment, then he throws it on him."
"9304","(9304) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is disliked for a fasting person to sprinkle his bed with water, then He sleeps on it."
"9305","(9305) Azhar Al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Ibn Sirin did not see any harm in getting a garment wet, then He meets him on his face."
"9306","(9306) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Othman bin Abi Al-Aas; He used to pour water on him and relieve him while he was fasting on the evening of Arafat, or the day of Arafat."
"9307","(9307) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, he said: I saw Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad soaking his feet in water. And he is fasting."
"9308","(9308) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Sumayyah, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abdul Rahman ibn al-Harith, on the authority of a man He saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, pouring water on his head while he was fasting, on a summer day. (Abu Dawud 2357. Ahmad 3/43)"
"9309","(9309) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It was disliked for a fasting person to wet his clothes. With water, then he puts it on."
"9310","(9310) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, never fasted for ten days."
"9311","(9311) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: I did not see the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he never fasted for ten days. (Muslim 10. Abu Dawud 2431)"
"9312","(9312) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad used to fast the entire ten days of Dhul-Hijjah. The ten days had passed and the days of Tashreeq had passed. He broke his fast for nine days in the same manner as he had fasted."
"9313","(9313) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Laith, he said: Mujahid used to fast the ten days, he said: And he A gift that costs her."
"9314","(9314) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of al-Nu’man ibn Sa’d, who said: A man came to Ali and said: O Commander of the Faithful, he informed me about a month that I will fast after Ramadan. He said: You have asked me about something that I have not heard from anyone. He asks about him, after a man I heard asking the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about him, and he said to him: If you are fasting A month after Ramadan is the fast of Muharram, for it is the month of God, and in it is a day in which some people repent, and in it others are repented. (Tirmidhi 741, Dharmi 1756)"
"9315","(9315) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to fast during the sacred months."
"9316","(9316) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Uthman, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yasar, and his brother Salit. They said: Ibn Omar was in Mecca and fasted during the months of the Sacred Mosque."
"9317","(9317) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umayr, on the authority of Muhammad bin al-Muntashir, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman Al-Himyari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: : O Messenger of God, which fast is best after Ramadan? He said: The month of God whom you call is Muharram. (Muslim 2031, Abu Dawud 2421)"
"9318","(9318) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays."
"9319","(9319) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Hafsa; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays. (Abu Dawud 2443. Ahmad 6/287)"
"9320","(9320) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sulayman al-Absi, on the authority of Mujahid; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays."
"9321","(9321) Othman bin Matar narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, on the authority of Abu Uqba, who said: Abu Hurairah used to fast Monday and Thursday."
"9322","(9322) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; He used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays."
"9323","(9323) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I asked him about fasting on Mondays and Thursdays? He said: I don't know of any harm in it."
"9324","(9324) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed; Omar bin Abdul Aziz used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays."
"9325","(9325) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Mujahid; He used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays, but then he disliked that."
"9326","(9326) Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Hisham Al-Dastawai informed us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Omar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban, that his servant in front of him narrated to him: That his master, Usama, narrated to him: That Usama was going out to He has property in Wadi al-Qura, so he fasts on Mondays and Thursdays. So I said to him: Why do you fast on Mondays and Thursdays when you are old? Big? He said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fasting on them, so I said to him: Why do you fast on Mondays and Thursdays? He said: These are two days in which deeds will be presented. (Abu Dawud 2428. Ahmad 5/200)"
"9327","(9327) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, who said: Usama bin Zaid was He fasted several days on Friday, following them, and he was asked: Where are you from Monday and Thursday? He said: He used to fast them both."
"9328","(9328) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zur, on the authority of Abdullah; He used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays."
"9329","(9329) Asbat bin Muhammad and Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He was asked about fasting on Mondays and Thursdays? He said: It is disliked to set aside a day for fasting. However, Yazid said: It is placed in the accusative case. One day, when that day comes, he fasts on it."
"9330","(9330) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas; Ali used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays."
"9331","(9331) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sulayman al-Absi, on the authority of Mujahid; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays."
"9332","(9332) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: None of you should fast on Friday unless he fasts before it, or fasts after it. (Muslim 148 Abu Dawud 2412)"
"9333","(9333) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith on the day of Friday while she was fasting. He said: So he said Yesterday was silent? She said: No. He said: Do you want to fast tomorrow? She said: No, he said: Then break your fast. (Ahmad 2/1891 Ibn Hibban 3611)"
"9334","(9334) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Marthad bin Abdullah Al-Yazani, on the authority of Hudhaifa Al-Azdi, on the authority of Junada Al-Azdi; I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with seven people of Azd. I was the eighth of them on the day of Friday and we were fasting. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for some food to be had and we said: We are fasting. He said: Did you fast yesterday? We said: No. He said: Will you fast tomorrow? We said: No. He said: So they broke their fast. Then he went out to the Friday prayer meeting, and when he sat on the pulpit, he called for a vessel of water and they drank it, and the people They look at him, to teach them that he does not fast on Friday. (Nasa’i 2774 and Hakim 608)"
"9335","(9335) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Imran bin Dhabyan, on the authority of Hakim bin Saad, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib May God have mercy on him, he said: Whoever of you has voluntary days of the month, let them fast on Thursday, and do not He fasts on Friday, for it is a day of food, drink, and remembrance, so he brings together two righteous days for God, the day of fasting. And the day we perform ritual sacrifice with the Muslims."
"9336","(9336) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Qais bin Sakan, who said Some of Abdullah Ali’s companions passed by Abu Dharr on the day of Friday while they were fasting, and he said: I swore to you that you would break your fast. Eid day."
"9337","(9337) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Do not fast on Friday deliberately."
"9338","(9338) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: Do not fast on Friday, unless you fast the day before or after it."
"9339","(9339) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi; He hated to fast on Friday, so he baptized it alone."
"9340","(9340) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Indeed, they disliked fasting on Friday so that they may strengthen themselves in prayer thereby."
"9341","(9341) Shababah ibn Siwar told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Ayyub al-Atkiki, on the authority of Juwayriyah; That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon her while she was fasting on Friday, and said: Did you remain silent yesterday? She said: No, he said: Will you fast tomorrow? She said: No, he said: Then break your fast. (Bukhari 1986. Ahmad 6/430)"
"9342","(9342) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Ziyad al-Harithi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: He has a man: Are you the one who forbids fasting on Friday? He said: No, by the Lord of this sanctuary, or this building, I have not forbidden it. Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said (Nasa’i 2744, Ahmad 2/526)"
"9343","(9343) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Walid Ibn Muslim, on the authority of Husayn Ibn Abi Al-Hurr, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn? He said: Do not fast on a day that makes it obligatory for you to fast. It is not part of Ramadan."
"9344","(9344) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Ibn Abbas forbade the Today, everything that happened to a person, and about fasting the specified days, and he forbade fasting for months, they did not make a mistake."
"9345","(9345) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They hated to impose an imposition on themselves. Something that was not imposed on them."
"9346","(9346) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin? He said: Do not single out the day of Friday as a fast between the days, nor the night of Friday as a night of prayer between the nights."
"9347","(9347) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He hated to miss a month or a day to fast."
"9348","(9348) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They hated to be castrated on Friday. And the same night with prayer."
"9349","(9349) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir (h) and on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; They both hated to fast a day at two times."
"9350","(9350) Ubaidullah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid? He said: Do not fast an entire month to compare it to the month of Ramadan, and do not fast a single day out of the crowd lest you consider it a holiday. Unless you fast before or after it."
"9351","(9351) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: I have never seen him breaking the fast on the day of Friday prayer."
"9352","(9352) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Umair bin Abi Umair, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I did not see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, he never breaks the fast on Friday. (Abu Ali 5709)"
"9353","(9353) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, he breaks his fast on Friday. (Tirmidhi 742, Abu Dawud 2442)"
"9354","(9354) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’, he said: I asked Abraham about snuff with patience for a fasting person? He saw no harm in it."
"9355","(9355) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in snuff for the fasting person, and he disliked pouring it into the ear."
"9356","(9356) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; It is disliked for the fasting person to be thirsty."
"9357","(9357) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Harith, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He dislikes snuff for the fasting person."
"9358","(9358) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: What is the use of patience for the fasting person? He said: Yes, if he wishes."
"9359","(9359) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in kohl for the fasting person."
"9360","(9360) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in using kohl for the fasting person."
"9361","(9361) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in kohl for a fasting person as long as he does not taste it."
"9362","(9362) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, Muhammad bin Ali, and Ata’; Indeed, they used to apply anticonvulsive kohl while fasting, and they did not see any harm in it."
"9363","(9363) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in using kohl. For the fasting person"
"9364","(9364) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Muadh, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Abi Bakr, on the authority of Anas; He used to apply kohl while fasting."
"9365","(9365) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, Abu Hilal, and his followers; They disliked kohl for the fasting person."
"9366","(9366) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He did not see any harm in a man using kohl while he was fasting."
"9367","(9367) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There is no harm in using kohl for the fasting person."
"9368","(9368) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, or Ata, who said: There is no harm for a fasting person to eat from pot."
"9369","(9369) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no harm in tasting vinegar. Or the thing unless it enters his throat while he is fasting."
"9370","(9370) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no harm for a fasting person to eat from Destiny"
"9371","(9371) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He saw no harm in a fasting person eating honey, ghee and the like, and then offering him food."
"9372","(9372) Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, on the authority of al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, who said: I saw Urwa ibn al-Zubayr fasting for a few days. And he tastes honey."
"9373","(9373) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: I asked the ruling about a fasting person who licks the filth. He said: There is no harm in it."
"9374","(9374) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Masruq, who said: I and a man with me came to Aisha. On that day, she called for a drink for us, then said: If I had not been fasting, I would have tasted it."
"9375","(9375) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, who said: There is no harm in a fasting person treating his gums."
"9376","(9376) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who has a wound and an ailment on his mouth, he said: There is no harm in applying wolfberry and similar medicines on him."
"9377","(9377) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Yahya bin Atiq, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Concerning a man who had a thrush on his lips, he said: There is no harm in wolfberries."
"9378","(9378) Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A man should not voluntarily fast while he is obligated to fast any of the following: Ramadan."
"9379","(9379) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He disliked voluntarily fasting while he had to make up for it from Ramadan, except the ten days."
"9380","(9380) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: The example of one who does voluntary prayers. He is obligated to make up for the missed days of Ramadan, like one who recites the tasbih but is afraid that he will miss what is obligatory for him."
"9381","(9381) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, who said: Suleiman bin Yasar and Saeed bin Al-Musayyab were asked about a man Did he volunteer and does he have to make up for the missed days of Ramadan? She thought about that."
"9382","(9382) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If a man has a judge from[corrupt] Ramadan and he volunteered it, then he made it up for it, even if he did not want it."
"9383","(9383) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Mughith asked Ata: Does a man insert something? He said: No."
"9384","(9384) A partner told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; He was asked about injections for the fasting person? He said: It is disliked for the one who breaks the fast, but it is sufficient for the fasting person."
"9385","(9385) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in a woman chewing for her son. She is fasting, as long as it does not enter her throat."
"9386","(9386) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: There is no harm in a woman chewing for her child. She is fasting."
"9387","(9387) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of al-Hasan; He did not see any harm in a fasting person littering himself with dung."
"9388","(9388) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in the offspring of a fasting person."
"9389","(9389) Muhammad ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, who said: A group of the people of Basra, some of them, testified with me. Al-Hasan bin Abi Al-Hasan Al-Basri, on the authority of Maqil bin Sinan Al-Ashja’i, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by me while I was He performed cupping on the eighteenth of Ramadan, and he said: The cupper and the one being cupped break his fast. (Tahawi 98. Ahmad 3/474)"
"9390","(9390) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Asim Al-Ahwal informed us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, who is Abu Qalab, On the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath Al-San’ani, on the authority of Abu Asma’ Al-Rahbi, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, who said: I passed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said the salutation on the eighteenth day of Ramadan, and he saw a man who had cupped, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The cupper broke his fast. And the stoned one. (Abu Dawud 2361. Ahmad 4/124)"
"9391","(9391) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Abi Asma’ al-Rahbi, on the authority of Shaddad ibn Aws, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the same. (Ahmad 4/124)"
"9392","(9392) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of the one who told him, on the authority of Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: He came The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a man using al-Baqi’ for cupping while holding his hand for the eighteen days that had passed during Ramadan. He said: The cupper and the one being performed have broken their fast. (Abu Dawud 2361. Ahmad 4/125)"
"9393","(9393) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: A man from the neighborhood, Mosaddeq, told me, on the authority of Thawban, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The cupper and the one being operated on break the fast. (Abu Dawud 2362. Ahmad 5/282)"
"9394","(9394) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ayoub Abu Al-Ala told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, On the authority of Bilal, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The cupper and the one being operated on break the fast. (Ahmad 6/12. Tabarani 1122)"
"9395","(9395) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God Almighty be pleased with him, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The cupper and the one being operated on break the fast. (Nasa’i 3172. Ahmad 6/364)"
"9396",""
"9397","(9397) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Ali said: The hajm broke the fast. And the stoned one."
"9398","(9398) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: It is disliked for the cupper and the one being operated on."
"9399","(9399) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Bakr, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, who said: I entered upon Abu Musa. He was the Emir of Basra in the evening, and I found him eating dates and dates, and he had cupped, so I said to him: Don’t you use cupping during the day? He said: Do you command me to shed my blood while I am fasting?"
"9400","(9400) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Talq ibn Habib, who said: The cupper and the one being treated break the fast."
"9401","(9401) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The fasting person should not use cupping."
"9402","(9402) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The cupper and the one having the procedure break his fast."
"9403","(9403) Yahya bin Ya’li told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The fasting person should not use cupping."
"9404","(9404) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed cupping between Mecca and Medina, in ihram and fasting. (Tirmidhi 777. Abu Dawud 2365)"
"9405","(9405) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had cupping while he was fasting."
"9406","(9406) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used cupping while fasting. (Nasa’i 3224. Ahmad 1/286)"
"9407","(9407) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had cupping while he was fasting. (Nasa’i 3222. Abd al-Razzaq 7536)"
"9408","(9408) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata bin Yasar He raised it and said: There are three things that do not break the fast: Cupping, vomiting, and wet dreams. (Abdul Razzaq 7539. Ibn Khuzaymah 1976)"
"9409","(9409) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Aban ibn Salih, on the authority of Muslim ibn Sa’id, he said: Ibn Masoud was asked About cupping for the fasting person? He said: There is no harm in it."
"9410","(9410) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: Anas was asked about cupping for a fasting person? He said: We did not consider anything objectionable from that except his effort."
"9411","(9411) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Regarding cupping for the fasting person, he said: Breaking the fast is from what comes in, not from what comes out."
"9412","(9412) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: He used to use cupping while fasting, then He left her after that, and he was using cupping at night."
"9413","(9413) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to use cupping at night while fasting."
"9414","(9414) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: There is no harm in cupping. For the fasting person"
"9415","(9415) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa’id; He dislikes cupping for the fasting person because of weakness."
"9416","(9416) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abdullah Al-Jarami, on the authority of a dinar. He said: Zayd bin Arqam was cupped. And he is fasting."
"9417","(9417) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Asama, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Al-Hussein bin Ali was cupped while he was Fasting"
"9418","(9418) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, and Tawus; Indeed, they did not see any harm in cupping for the fasting person."
"9419","(9419) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, who said: I saw Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Salami cupping while he was fasting while he was fasting. The setting of the sun, in a way that agreed with his natural condition, so I said to him: O Abu Abdul Rahman; Cupping is only disliked for the fasting person. He said: Cupping is only disliked for him due to fear of weakness."
"9420","(9420) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, only forbade cupping for the fasting person. And the connection in fasting is to protect one’s companions. (Abu Dawud 2366. Ahmad 4/314)"
"9421","(9421) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Buzai’, he said: I asked Abu Wa’il about cupping for a fasting person? He said: This is disliked because of weakness."
"9422","(9422) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Ahwas bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Jubair bin Nufayr; Mu'adh had cupping while he was fasting."
"9423","(9423) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman, on the authority of Ata’ and Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: There is no problem. Cupping is for the fasting person as long as he does not fear weakness."
"9424","(9424) Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim, and Salem, similarly."
"9425","(9425) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: A man asked Ikrimah about cupping for a fasting person? He said: There is no problem with it, but it is something like such-and-such and such-and-such that comes out of you. He mentioned the pilgrim."
"9426","(9426) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father; He used to use cupping while fasting."
"9427","(9427) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Furat, on the authority of a servant of Umm Salama; He saw Umm Salama using cupping while she was fasting."
"9428","(9428) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid, and Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; That he used to perform cupping while fasting, then he abandoned that, so I do not know for what reason he abandoned it? Hate, or weakness."
"9429","(9429) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Warith, on the authority of Anas, who said: Abu Tayyab passed by us and said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was cupped while he was fasting. (Tirmidhi 366 and Abu Ali 4210)"
"9430","(9430) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abu Ja`far; Cupping is disliked for the fasting person due to fear of weakness."
"9431","(9431) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a woman who menstruates at the beginning of the day during the month of Ramadan, and he said: She eats and drinks."
"9432","(9432) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a woman who menstruated after the sun turned yellow in Ramadan. He said: That breaks the fast. He said: And if she became menstruating, then she broke the fast after sunrise. Fajr? He said: Do not eat the rest of your day."
"9433","(9433) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; In a woman who fasts at the beginning of the day, then she menstruates. He said: She eats."
"9434","(9434) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; During the menstruating woman, she purifies herself and does not eat anything. It is disliked for her to resemble the polytheists until the night."
"9435","(9435) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Abdullah said: Whoever eats at the beginning of the day, let him eat. The last one"
"9436","(9436) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Concerning a man who came in Ramadan on the first day of the day and had eaten. He said: He does not eat the rest of his day."
"9437","(9437) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; What about a traveler arriving after he had eaten? He said: He does not eat the rest of his day. Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: He does not eat his hatred to imitate the polytheists, until the night."
"9438","(9438) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Harith, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If a traveler enters Egypt, he does not eat anything. Even if he ate before serving."
"9439","(9439) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to a man who had intercourse with his family during Ramadan: If he blew your back, then do not do so. Your stomach"
"9440","(9440) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning the one who befalls his family, meaning in the month of Ramadan, he said: If he wishes, he may eat and drink."
"9441","(9441) Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Amr ibn Dinar: Isn’t this what is said about what Is it affliction with his family during Ramadan, to complete that day and complete it? He said: Yes."
"9442","(9442) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He used to say: If he fainted, he did not care whether he ate or not. He eats it"
"9443","(9443) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sayfi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to us: May God bless him and grant him peace. On the day of Ashura: Has anyone among you tasted the food of today? So we said: Some of us ate, and some of us did not. He said: So he said: Complete the rest of your day, those who ate, and those who did not. And they sent for the people of the offerings to complete the rest of their day, meaning the people of the offerings around the city. (Nasa’i 2629)"
"9444","(9444) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Musa, He said: The Day of Ashura is a day that the Jews venerate and take as a festival. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Fast on it. You? (Bukhari 2005, Muslim 130)"
"9445","(9445) Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Mujazi’ bin Zahir, on the authority of his father, he said: He ordered The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recommended fasting on the Day of Ashura."
"9446","(9446) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hijri, on the authority of Abu Iyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The Day of Ashura is a day on which the prophets used to fast, so fast on it you too. (Bazzar 1046)"
"9447","(9447) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Ubaid Allah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; The people of the pre-Islamic era used to fast on the day of Ashura, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fasted. And the Muslims before Ramadan was established, and when Ramadan was assumed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, Ashura It is one of the days of God, so whoever wishes may fast it, and whoever wishes may leave it. (Bukhari 4501, Muslim 792)"
"9448","(9448) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: He was Ashura. One day the Quraysh fasted during the pre-Islamic era. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina, he fasted and ordered By fasting, then when Ramadan was imposed, Ramadan was the obligatory one, and he left off Ashura, so whoever wishes may fast it, and whoever wishes may leave it.\n(Muslim 792. Abu Dawud 2434)"
"9449","(9449) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Shayban informed us, on the authority of Ash’ath ibn Abi Al-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Abi Thawr, on the authority of Jabir bin Samarra, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to command us to fast on Ashura and urge us to fast. upon him, or he will get along with us, so when Ramadan was imposed, he did not command us, nor did he forbid us from it, nor did we get along with him. With him \n(Muslim 125 Ahmad 5/105)"
"9450","(9450) Shababi told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina while the Jews were fasting on the Day of Ashura, he asked them about that? They said: This is the day on which Moses appeared against Pharaoh, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Because you have more right to Moses. Of them, fast them. (Bukhari 4737 and Muslim 796)"
"9451","(9451) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd, who said: Al-Ash’ath ibn Qais came to Abdullah while he was having lunch, and he said: O Abu Muhammad, come closer to lunch. He said: Isn’t today the day of Ashura? ? He said: Do you know what Ashura Day is? He said: What is it? He said: It is a day on which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was fasting before the month of Ramadan began. When it came The month of Ramadan was abandoned. (Muslim 122. Ahmad 1/424)"
"9452","(9452) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: I have not seen anyone who commanded fasting on the Day of Resurrection. Ashura from Ali bin Abi Talib and Abi Musa."
"9453","(9453) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, and Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: I have not seen anyone command By fasting on the day of Ashura from Ali bin Abi Talib and Abu Musa."
"9454","(9454) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali; He used to order fasting on the day of Ashura."
"9455","(9455) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdul-Malik informed me, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Al-Rahman bin Al-Harith; Omar sent a message to Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith on the evening of the night of Ashura: “They had the suhoor meal and he was fasting in the morning, and Abd al-Rahman was fasting in the morning.”"
"9456","(9456) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of al-Qasim; He used to fast on Ashura."
"9457","(9457) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymara, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Qays ibn Saad, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered fasting on the Day of Ashura. (Ahmad 421. An-Nasa’i 3/2841)"
"9458","(9458) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Qasim; When Ramadan came, he did not command us, nor did he prohibit us, but we will do it."
"9459","(9459) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded a man who converted to Islam on the day of Ashura, and said: Go to your people and tell them to fast this month. Today, he said: I do not want me to come to them until they wake up, so he said: Order whoever of them wakes up to fast for the rest of the day. And whoever among them does not wake up must fast. (Abdul Razzaq 7834)"
"9460","(9460) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to fast."
"9461","(9461) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; It was astonishing for him to fast on the day of Ashura."
"9462","(9462) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Qais bin Sakan; Al-Ash'ath came to Abdullah on the day of Ashura while he was eating food, and he said: Come closer and eat. He said: I am fasting, so he said: It was only This was before Ramadan came."
"9463","(9463) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim; Omar did not fast."
"9464","(9464) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Qais bin Sakan al-Asadi, on the authority of Abdullah Like him, except that he said: Come closer and eat."
"9465","(9465) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Yahya bin Abdullah bin Sayfi told me that Amr bin Abi Yusuf, the brother of Banu Nawfal, told him that he heard Muawiyah say on the pulpit: The day of Ashura is the day of Eid, so whoever wishes may fast, and he used to fast, and whoever wishes may leave it, and there is no blame."
"9466","(9466) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Walid, who said: Ikrimah was asked about fasting on the day of Ashura. And the day of Arafah? He said: It is not appropriate for a man to fast on a day that he feels is obligatory for him, except Ramadan."
"9467","(9467) Ali bin Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Bishr, who said: I heard Ali ordering the Ashura fast."
"9468","(9468) Ali bin Musahir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: Abu Mawiya told me, he said: I heard Ali say about fasting. Ashura: Whoever begins, let him complete, and whoever eats, let him fast."
"9469","(9469) Ali bin Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, on the authority of Abu Qatada, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Fasting the day of Ashura is atonement for one year, and fasting the day of Arafat is atonement for two years. A past year and a future year. (Nasa’i 2809. Ahmad 5/307)"
"9470","(9470) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid, he heard Ibn Abbas asked about fasting on Ashura? He said: I did not know that I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fast a single day, asking for his spare days except This day, and there is no month except this, meaning Ramadan. (Bukhari 2006, Muslim 131)"
"9471","(9471) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He used to fast the day before and after it, for fear that he would miss it."
"9472","(9472) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Hajib ibn Umar, on the authority of al-Hakam ibn al-Araj, who said: I came to Ibn Abbas while he was laying on a pillow. His robe in Zamzam, so I said: Tell me about fasting on Ashura? He said: If you see the crescent of Muharram, count, and on the morning of fasting the ninth, I said: This is how Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, was. Is he fasting? He said: Yes.\n(Muslim 132. Tirmidhi 754)"
"9473","(9473) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of al-Qasim ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If I stay until Qabil, I will fast the ninth, meaning the day of Ashura. (Muslim 133. Ahmad 224)"
"9474","(9474) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Sulayman, the client of Yahya bin Yamar, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas He says: The day of Ashura is the ninth morning and the tenth night."
"9475","(9475) Waki’ and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Salama, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Ashura is the ninth day."
"9476","(9476) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad. They said: Ashura is the tenth day."
"9477","(9477) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, al-Hasan, and Ikrimah. They said: Ashura is the tenth day."
"9478","(9478) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The tenth day."
"9479","(9479) Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Al-Araj, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It is the day The ninth"
"9480","(9480) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed me, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to fast on the day of Ashura while travelling, and he would go back and forth between the two days for fear that he would miss it."
"9481","(9481) Yazid told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Ashura is the tenth day."
"9482","(9482) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Al-Alaqah, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Prophet May the peace and blessings of God be upon him during the month of fasting. (Muslim 778. Abu Dawud 2375)"
"9483","(9483) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He kisses some of his wives while he is fasting, and she laughed, so we thought it was her. (Muslim 69)"
"9484","(9484) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, and Al-Alqamah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he kisses while he is fasting, and he kisses his face while he is fasting, but he was your master for his master. (Bukhari 1927, Muslim 68)"
"9485","(9485) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: There is no harm in kissing the fasting person."
"9486","(9486) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mubashir, on the authority of Zaid Abi Attab, who said: Saad was asked about the qiblah of a fasting person? He said: I took it from her while I was fasting."
"9487","(9487) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa’id; He was asked about the qiblah of the fasting person? He said: There is no problem with her, as long as that is not the case."
"9488","(9488) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Shutair ibn Shikal, on the authority of Hafsa bint Omar, who said: It was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, kissed while he was fasting. (Muslim 779. Tabarani 393)"
"9489","(9489) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Farukh, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: The Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He kisses me while I am fasting, and he is fasting. (Tabarani 654, Ahmad 6/320)"
"9490","(9490) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Habib Ibn Shihab, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He was asked about The kiss for the fasting person? He said: I like to have her lips while I am fasting."
"9491","(9491) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama, On the authority of Zainab bint Umm Salama, on the authority of Umm Salama, she said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss her while he was fasting."
"9492","(9492) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He was asked about the qiblah of the fasting person? He said: There is no harm in it."
"9493","(9493) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Muwarriq, who said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the qiblah of a fasting person? So he granted it."
"9494","(9494) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I asked Ikrimah and Al-Shu’abi about qiblah and directness. For the fasting person? So he made it easy for them."
"9495","(9495) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about the qiblah of a fasting person? He said: There is no harm in it, but it is bad mail."
"9496","(9496) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdullah bin Juma’, who said: I asked Abu Salamah about the kiss of a fasting person? He said: I kiss the Kalbiyya while I am fasting."
"9497","(9497) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Dhurayh, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Aisha She said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not refrain from coming to me while I was fasting. (Ahmad 6/213)"
"9498","(9498) Shababi told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Bukair ibn al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Sa`id al-Ansari, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, said: I went to the mirror and kissed her while I was fasting. He said: Then the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: What do you think if you rinse your mouth with water while you are fasting? He said: I said: No problem. He said: So what? (Abu Dawud 2377. Ahmad 1/52)"
"9499","(9499) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, he said: Sa’id bin Mardanbah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Kathir, on the authority of Umm She greeted him, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, because she said to him: If I approached, if I kissed, and he got married in Ramadan."
"9500","(9500) Yazeed told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid Allah bin Omar; Atika bint Zaid, the wife of Omar bin Al-Khattab, kissed him while he was fasting, but he did not prohibit her."
"9501","(9501) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Saleh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Muslim bin Hayyan, on the authority of Masruq; Concerning the kiss for the fasting person, he said: I don’t care whether I kissed her, or whether I kissed his hand."
"9502","(9502) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab; Omar forbade the fasting person from kissing."
"9503","(9503) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ubaid bin Amr, who said: A man said to Ali: Does a man kiss? His wife while he is fasting? Ali said: What confuses you about the contents of your wife’s mouth?"
"9504","(9504) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Al-Hazzaz; That a man met Ibn Masoud while he was practicing exercises, and he asked him about a fasting person before? He said: Break your fast."
"9505","(9505) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Will you not kiss his burning coal?"
"9506","(9506) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Muwarriq, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about the qiblah of a fasting person? He forbade it."
"9507","(9507) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated it for a man to kiss his wife while he was fasting."
"9508","(9508) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I asked Ibn Mughaffal? He thought about it."
"9509","(9509) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim (h), Jarir, and Waki’, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, both of them on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh said: He was asked about the qiblah of a fasting person? He said: He fears God and does not go back."
"9510","(9510) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; He said in the Qibla to the fasting person: His fast is broken, and he does not break his fast with it."
"9511","(9511) Shababā told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, who said: I heard alcohol being consumed, and a young man came to him and said: I kiss in it. It was the month of Ramadan and I was fasting. He said: My son, I will do that, but you will not do it."
"9512","(9512) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ibn Shubarmah, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, who said: Kiss invalidates ablution and hurts Fasting"
"9513","(9513) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Habib, who said: I asked Abu Qalabi about the qiblah of a fasting person? He said: Do not kiss while you are fasting."
"9514","(9514) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah; He was asked about the qiblah of the fasting person? He said: What do you do without fear?"
"9515","(9515) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: It was disliked to kiss the fasting person."
"9516","(9516) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Omar bin Hamza, he said: Salem informed me, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: Omar said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a dream, and I saw him not looking at me, so I said: O Messenger of God, what is the matter with you? He said: Aren't you the one who kisses while you are fasting? He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not kiss her after that while I am fasting."
"9517","(9517) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Hafsiya, on the authority of Abi Ya’la, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah said: Fasting is only a form of desire, and kissing is a form of desire."
"9518","(9518) Shababah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Tha’labah bin Abdullah bin Abi Su’air, He said: I saw the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they forbade the fasting person from kissing."
"9519","(9519) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Yazid Al-Dunni, On the authority of Maymunah, his servant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about a fasting person before? He said: Break your fast. (Ahmad 6/463. Tabarani 57)"
"9520","(9520) His youth narrated to us, he said: Shu’ba narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Masruq; He was asked about the qiblah of the fasting person? He said: The night is near."
"9521","(9521) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, and Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: It was The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to eat food while fasting, but he was your guardian to his master."
"9522","(9522) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Salim Al-Awsi, he said: A man said to Saad: O Abu Ishaq, do you have sexual intercourse while you are fasting? He said: Yes, and he took it."
"9523","(9523) Ali bin Musahir and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Abu Misra, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, He said: He used to have intercourse with his wife in the middle of the day while he was fasting."
"9524","(9524) Hafs told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A Bedouin came to him and asked him? So he gave him permission to kiss, to touch, and to put on the hand, as long as he did not promise anything else."
"9525","(9525) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Makin, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no harm for the sheikh to communicate. That is, while he was fasting."
"9526","(9526) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I asked Ikrimah and Al-Shu’abi about direct contact? So they made some concessions regarding it, and I asked the son of a fool? He thought about it."
"9527","(9527) Abdah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Bura, who said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: I will be intimate with my wife. And I am fasting? He said: No, then another came and said: Should I have intercourse with my wife while I am fasting? He said: Yes, and it was said to him: O Abu Abdul Rahman, you said yes to this man, and you said no to this man? He said: This is an old man and this is a young man."
"9528","(9528) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It was said to Ibn Abbas: Al-Mubashara? He said: Pardon your fasting."
"9529","(9529) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He hated kissing and being intimate."
"9530","(9530) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, he said: Hanzali bin Sabra bin Al-Musayyab bin Najab informed us Al-Fazariy, on the authority of his paternal aunt Jumana bint Al-Musayyab, who was with Hudhayfah ibn Al-Yaman, so when he prayed the dawn prayer in Ramadan He entered with her in her quilt, and he put his back on her to keep himself warm near her, and not to kiss her."
"9531","(9531) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he said: When he is called If one of you comes to food while he is fasting, let him say: I am fasting."
"9532","(9532) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I entered upon Qais bin Abi Hazim, and he called for me a drink, and he said: Drink. I said: I do not want to. He said: Are you fasting? I said: Yes, he said: For I heard Abdullah say: If one of you is offered food or drink while he is fasting, let him say: I am. Fasting"
"9533","(9533) Waki’ and Yazid narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If one of you is asked and he He is fasting, so let him say: I am fasting."
"9534","(9534) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: When Ibn Umar was invited to eat while he was fasting, he would respond. So, when they brought the table with food on it, he extended his hand and said: Take it in the name of God. If the people seek refuge, He will desist. His hand"
"9535","(9535) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Qays ibn Abi Hazim, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: If he is presented If one of you needs food or drink while he is fasting, let him say: I am fasting."
"9536","(9536) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, he said: Food was brought to Anas, and he said to him: I bow down, so I said: I do not feed, and he said: What: I do not feed? Say: I am fasting."
"9537","(9537) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhazim, he said: Abu Hurairah said: If one of you is asked: Are you fasting? Let him say: I am fasting. As for the believer, he will pray for good for him. As for the hypocrite, he will say: Hypocritical."
"9538","(9538) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Imran bin Hudayr told us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, he said: I entered upon him. And he was eating, so he said: Come closer and eat. He said: I said: I am fasting. He said: Perhaps you are among those who claim that he is fasting and he is not fasting. I said: Glory be to God. He said: Someone better than you would fast three days of every month, then say: I am fasting."
"9539","(9539) Abu Al-Ahwas Salam bin Sulaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: I saw Al-Sha’bi entering the bathroom while he was fasting."
"9540","(9540) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I asked Abu Al-Aaliyah: Should I enter the bathroom while I am fasting? He said: Do you like to look at your private parts while you are fasting? He said: I said: Should I enter the bathroom wearing an apron? He said: Would you like to look at someone else's private parts while you are fasting? He said: I said: No."
"9541","(9541) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Do not enter the bathroom while you are fasting."
"9542","(9542) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, who said: I saw the crescent, the crescent of Al-Fitr, close to Zuhr prayer, and some people broke their fast, so we came to Anas bin Malik, and we mentioned to him the sighting of the crescent and the breaking of the fast by those who had broken the fast. He said : As for me, I will complete this day until night."
"9543","(9543) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Concerning the crescent is seen by daylight: Do not break your fast until you see it from where it is seen."
"9544","(9544) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, he said: The people broke their fast, so I went to Abu Wael and said: I saw The crescent moon is the middle of the day, so he said: {Complete the fast until the night}"
"9545","(9545) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala; People saw the crescent of the breaking of the fast when the sun had risen, and some of them broke the fast. I mentioned that to Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, and he said: The people saw it in the time of Othman, and some of them broke their fast. Then Othman stood up and said: As for me, I will continue my fast until nightfall. He said: It was seen in... The time of Marwan, so Marwan threatened who would break his fast. Sa’id said: So Marwan did so."
"9546","(9546) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman, who said: Abdullah said: When you see the crescent By day, do not break your fast, for its course is in the heavens, perhaps it will be the people of that time."
"9547","(9547) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: When you see the crescent at the beginning of the day, do not break your fast, and when you see him at the end of the day, break your fast."
"9548","(9548) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of his father, he said: We were with Salman bin Rabi`a in Balanjar, and we saw the crescent of Shawwal on the twenty-nine day of noon, so he said: Show me it, so I showed it to him, so he ordered the people So they broke their fast."
"9549","(9549) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Farroukh, on the authority of Salih Ad-Dahhan, who said: The crescent was seen at the end of Ramadan during the day, and the people fell asleep. In food and drink, and a group of Azd were secluded, and they said: O Salih, you are our messenger to Jabir bin Zayd, so I came to Jabir bin Zaid, so I mentioned that to him, and he said: Are you among those who saw him? I said: Yes. He said: Did you see it in front of the sun, or did you see it behind it? I said: No, between her hands. He said: This is your day of Ramadan. You only saw it on its way, so pass by your companions. They complete their fasting and seclusion."
"9550","(9550) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Utba bin Farqad was absent in black, So they saw the crescent at the end of the day, so they broke their fast, and that time reached Omar, and it was written to him: When the crescent is seen at the beginning of the day, It is for the past day, so break your fast, and when it is seen at the end of the day, it is for the coming day, so complete the fast."
"9551","(9551) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ used to say: If the crescent of Shawwal is seen by day, then Break your fast, and he recites: {Then complete the fast until the night}."
"9552","(9552) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, who said: I saw the crescent before noon, so I went to Abu My cloak, so he ordered me to complete my fast."
"9553","(9553) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: Omar’s letter came to us while we were in Khanaqin; Some crescents are larger than others, so if you see the crescents during the day, do not break your fast, until two Muslim men bear witness. Indeed, they were worthy of it yesterday."
"9554","(9554) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Abu Umair ibn Anas, he said: My Ansar cousins narrated to me, they said: We fainted on the crescent of Shawwal, so we began fasting, then a group came at the end of the day, and they testified with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said that they saw the crescent yesterday, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the people to break their fast and go out to Their Eid from tomorrow. (Abu Dawud 1150. Ahmad 5/57)"
"9555","(9555) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ya’four, on the authority of his father, who said: The crescent of Ramadan was seen by Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba. Ali Al-Kufa, and he did not leave until it was the next day, so he went out and addressed the people on a camel, then he left."
"9556","(9556) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: It was reported by Ibn Umar that they saw the crescent, so he said: Go out. Until your feast tomorrow, and the day has passed as long as God wills."
"9557","(9557) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah; That a Bedouin testified with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the sighting of the crescent, and he said: Do you bear witness that there is no god but God? And I am the Messenger of God? He said: Yes, he said: So the people were ordered to fast. (Abu Dawud 2334. An-Nasa’i 2424)"
"9558","(9558) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila; Omar ibn al-Khattab permitted the testimony of a man in the crescent moon."
"9559","(9559) Ali bin Misir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Misir, who said: I witnessed Medina in The crescent is a sign of fasting or breaking the fast. No one bore witness to the crescent except a man, so Ibn Umar ordered them to do so and they accepted his testimony."
"9560","(9560) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He came A Bedouin went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, I saw the crescents last night. He said: You bear witness that There is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger? He said: Yes. He said: O Bilal, call upon the people to fast tomorrow. (Tirmidhi 691, Abu Dawud 233)"
"9561","(9561) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: He came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Two Arab men came, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: Are you Muslims? They said: Yes, so he said to them: Have you two? They said: Yes, so he ordered the people to break their fast, or to break their fast. (Daraqutni 167)"
"9562","(9562) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali; Concerning the crescent, he said: If two just men bear witness to the sighting of the crescent, then break the fast."
"9563","(9563) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, who said: Abu Uthman would permit it. Hashim bin Utbah, or someone else, bore witness to the sighting of the Crescent."
"9564","(9564) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say about a man who sees the crescent alone before the people. He said: He does not fast except with the people, and he does not break his fast except with the people. People"
"9565","(9565) Al-Dahhak narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who bore witness to the sighting of the crescent alone, he said: He should not pay attention to it."
"9566","(9566) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: We were in Khanaqin, so the crescent of Ramadan was shown to us, so among us were those who He fasted, and some of us broke the fast. Then the letter of Omar came to us: “Indeed, some of the crescents are greater than others, so if you see the crescents by day, then do not Break your fast, unless two Muslim men testify that they performed the ihram yesterday."
"9567","(9567) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir; That Muhammad bin Suwayd al-Fihri broke his fast, or sacrificed a day before the people, so Omar bin Abdulaziz wrote to him: What What made you break the fast before the people? So Muhammad wrote to him: He testified in the presence of Hizam bin Hakim al-Qurashi that he saw the crescent moon, so Omar wrote to him: Or One of the people, or one with two hands: He is."
"9568","(9568) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz; Some people bore witness to the crescent of Ramadan after the morning had passed, and he said: Whoever does not eat, let him complete his fast, and whoever does eat, let him complete his fast. Let him fast for the rest of his day."
"9569","(9569) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: What do you think if the people of Mecca break their fast in the morning? Or a man, or two men, then it came to them that the crescent moon had been seen, and the news of that came to them at the beginning of the day, or at the end. During the day, were they fasting for the rest of their day, or were they making up for it after that? He said: They can eat and drink if they want, but it is not obligatory for them to fast the rest of it."
"9570","(9570) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If the fasting person feels safe, then he has broken his fast."
"9571","(9571) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If the fasting person feels secure, he will break his fast. I said: It expiates. Atonement for semen? He said: Yes."
"9572","(9572) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he kisses or touches while he is fasting and feels safe, It is in the same position as the mosques."
"9573","(9573) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr ibn Harim, who said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked about a man who looked He went to his wife during Ramadan, so he was safe from her lust. Will he break his fast? He said: No, and he will complete his fast."
"9574","(9574) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir; Concerning a fasting person who plays with his wife until she vomits or performs intercourse. He said: It is not obligatory for him to make up anything except what it has been obligatory for him to do. Washing"
"9575","(9575) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If the fasting person wishes, he will break his fast."
"9576","(9576) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, who said: On the authority of Ibn Abbas (h) and on the authority of Harith, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, they said: If it is for something other than prayer, then it is made up for, and if it is for prayer, then it is not made up for."
"9577","(9577) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say: If he rinses his mouth while fasting and something enters his throat that he did not intend, then there is nothing wrong with him. fasting"
"9578","(9578) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Khaliq, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a fasting person rinsing his mouth, and water entered his throat. He said: If it was an obligatory ablution, then he does not have to do anything, but if it was an obligatory ablution, then he does not have to do anything. Change it, for it is a feast."
"9579","(9579) Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, a person said to Ata’: I blew my nose and water entered my throat, is there any problem? He said: It's okay, you don't have it."
"9580","(9580) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a fasting person who performs ablution and some of his ablution enters his throat. He said: If he remembers his fast, then he must make up for it, even if Forgetting, there is nothing wrong with him."
"9581","(9581) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr ibn Harim, who said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked about a man who was He was fasting, so he performed ablution, and the water rushed to his throat. Does he break his fast? He said: No, and let him complete his fast."
"9582","(9582) Hafs told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amer, who said: Ali and Omar had forbidden fasting on that day. There is doubt about Ramadan."
"9583","(9583) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Dharais, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abbas, on the authority of his father, who said: Abdullah said: Because If I break my fast one day of Ramadan, then make it up, that is more beloved to me than adding to it what is not part of it."
"9584","(9584) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz ibn Hakim, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: If the Sunnah were silent Both of them I would have broken my fast on the day of doubt."
"9585","(9585) Hafs and Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: Al-Dahhak bin Qais said: If I had fasted The entire Sunnah, I did not fast on the day of Ramadan in which there is doubt."
"9586","(9586) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of a servant of Salma bint Hudhayfah, on the authority of Bint Hudhayfah She said: Hudhayf had forbidden fasting on a day about which there was doubt."
"9587","(9587) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mahdi bin Maimun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: One day we woke up in Basra. We did not know what we were in for regarding our fasting on the day about which there was doubt, so we came to Anas bin Malik, and behold, And he had taken his khazira, which he had taken before morning, and then in the morning, then I came to Abu al-Sawwar al-Ataki and he called With his lunch, then he had lunch, then I came to Muslim bin Yassar and found him breaking his fast."
"9588","(9588) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Al-Shu’bi, that they said: Do not fast except with a group. People"
"9589","(9589) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no day that I fast that I hate more than A day in which people will disagree."
"9590","(9590) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of a woman among them, called: Hafsa, on the authority of a daughter or sister. To Hudhayfah, she said: Hudhayfiya forbade fasting on a day about which there was doubt."
"9591","(9591) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Eizar, who said: I came to Abraham on the day about which he was in doubt, and he said: Perhaps you are fasting, do not fast except in congregation."
"9592","(9592) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Qays, who said: I said to Al-Qasim: Do you detest the fast of the last day of Sha’ban, which follows? Ramadan? He said: No, unless the crescent moon becomes blind."
"9593","(9593) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He used to fast during the middle of the day. Because of the presence of a witness, or the presence of an absent person, if he comes, otherwise he breaks his fast."
"9594","(9594) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Al-Mu’alla, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; He hated to fast on the day that was different from Ramadan."
"9595","(9595) Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ruba’i, that Ammar ibn Yasir and people with him He brought them grilled slaughtered meat on a day on which there was doubt that it was from Ramadan, or not from Ramadan, so they gathered together. A man withdrew from them, and Ammar said to him: Come and eat. He said: For he is fasting, and Ammar said to him: If you believe in God and today Then come and eat."
"9596","(9596) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Whoever fasts on a day about which there is doubt He disobeyed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Abu Dawud 2327, Darmi 1682)"
"9597","(9597) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Aamir, who said: There is no day I hate to fast more than today. The one who doubts about Ramadan."
"9598","(9598) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amer; On the day that people say is Ramadan, he said: He said: Do not fast except with the imam, for it was the first group in Like this"
"9599","(9599) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibrahim; He said: There is no day that I hate to fast more than the day on which there is doubt than Ramadan."
"9600","(9600) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: Omar said: Let one of you beware of fasting. One day in Sha`ban, or he breaks the fast one day in Ramadan. If he comes before the people, then let him break his fast when the people break their fast."
"9601","(9601) Yazid told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman; He used to fast on the day of Ramadan in which there was doubt."
"9602","(9602) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Yafour, on the authority of Abu Al-Salt, on the authority of Abu Aqrab Al-Asadi, he said: We brought Ibn Masoud In his house, we found him above the House, and we heard him say before he came down: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. So when he came down, we said: Oh. Aba Abd al-Rahman, we heard you say: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth, and he said: Laylat al-Qadr is on the seventh of the other half, and that is because the sun That day it would appear white and without rays, so I looked at the sun and found it as it was described, so I magnified it."
"9603","(9603) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Omar, he said: You have known The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said regarding Laylat al-Qadr: Seek it in the last ten nights."
"9604","(9604) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Ubad ibn Al-Samit, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out against us. peace be upon him, and he wanted to inform us of Laylat al-Qadr, so two men approached me, and he said: I left and I wanted to I inform you of the Night of Decree, and so-and-so and so-and-so will face each other. Perhaps that will be good. Seek it on the ninth. And the seventh, and the fifth."
"9605","(9605) Shababi bin Siwar told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Khubayb, on the authority of Abdullah bin Anis, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he was asked about Laylat Destiny? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Search for it all night, and that night is three nights. And twenty."
"9606","(9606) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Marthad bin Abi Marthad, on the authority of his father; He said: I was with Abu Dharr at the middle Jamarat, and I asked him about Laylat al-Qadr? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to ask people about it. I said: O Messenger of God, tell us about it, and he said: If I had been given permission to do so, I would have told you, but seek it out during one of the seventy, and then do not ask me about it after you have stayed, or The position of this."
"9607","(9607) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Qannan bin Abdullah Al-Nahmi, who said: I asked Zurr bin Hubaish about Layla. Destiny? He said: Omar, Hudhayfah, and some of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had no doubt that it was Laylat. Twenty-seven. Zurr said: So continue with it."
"9608","(9608) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Qais, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar, who said: There is no harm in making up Ramadan on the ten days."
"9609","(9609) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Whoever is obligated to fast during Ramadan Do not make up for it in Dhul-Hijjah, for it is the month of rituals."
"9610","(9610) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Uthman ibn Mawhib, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: Begin with the obligatory prayer. There is no harm in fasting during the ten days."
"9611","(9611) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr (h) and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He begins with the obligatory fast. There is no harm in fasting it during the ten days."
"9612","(9612) Abdi told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab; He saw no harm in making up Ramadan on the ten days."
"9613","(9613) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in making up for Ramadan. The tithe"
"9614","(9614) Ismail told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawus, and Mujahid. They said: Make up Ramadan whenever you want, and Sa’id said. Ibn Jubayr: There is no harm in it."
"9615","(9615) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated it"
"9616","(9616) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I came during Ramadan while I was asleep. It was said: The night is the Night of Destiny. He said: I got up while I was sleepy and clung to some of the edges of the carpet of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace and blessings of God be upon him. So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying. I looked at the night and saw that it was night. Twenty-three. He said: Ibn Abbas said: Satan rises with the sun every day except Laylat al-Qadr. He said: And that. She will rise on that day without a ray of light."
"9617","(9617) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Jabalah, and Muharib, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Wait for Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten days, or he said: in the last seven days."
"9618","(9618) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Search for Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten nights. (Muslim 219. Ahmad 6/204)"
"9619","(9619) Abdul-Ala and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Marthad bin Abdullah Al-Yazani, on the authority of Al-Sanabihi, said: I asked Bilal about Laylat Al-Qadr? He said: The twenty-third night."
"9620","(9620) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his uncle, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I was shown the Night of Destiny and I forgot it, so seek it in the last ten nights, at times."
"9621","(9621) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: In Ramadan."
"9622","(9622) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Search the night. The fate is for seven to remain, move it for nine to remain, move it for eleven to remain, on the morning of a full moon, for the sun is rising Every day between the horns of Satan except the morning of Badr."
"9623","(9623) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Zirr, who said: I heard Ubayy bin Ka’b saying: Night. Al-Qadr is the twenty-seventh night."
"9624","(9624) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Hawt Al-Khuza’i, he said: I asked Zayd ibn Arqam about Laylatul Qadr? He said: He did not hesitate and had no doubt. He said: The night of the nineteenth, the night of disunity, the night of piety of the two groups."
"9625","(9625) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakra, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Seek Laylat al-Qadr on the ten days of Ramadan. For nine days, or for seven days, or for five, or for three, or for the last night."
"9626","(9626) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Zirr ibn Hubaysh, who said: I heard Ubayy say: Night. Destiny is the twenty-seventh night, the night that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed us that The sun rises white, sparkling."
"9627","(9627) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’ah ibn Kulthum, who said: I heard Al-Hasan say: Laylat Al-Qadr is in all of Ramadan."
"9628","(9628) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, who said: Laylat al-Qadr changed into ten nights."
"9629","(9629) Ibn Mahdi and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, who said: I heard a button say: Laylat al-Qadr is the twenty-seventh night, so if it is that night, then let each of you take a bath and break his fast with milk. And let him delay breaking his fast until dawn."
"9630","(9630) Affan told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Mu’awiyah, he said: Laylat al-Qadr. The twenty-third night."
"9631","(9631) Amr bin Hammad bin Talha told us, on the authority of Asbat bin Nasr, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten nights."
"9632","(9632) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Distawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abi Salamah, on the authority of Abi Saeed Al-Khudri said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: I was shown Laylat Al-Qadr but I forgot it. Or you have forgotten it, then seek it in the last ten days, in the odd night prayer. (Bukhari 813 and Abu Dawud 1377)"
"9633","(9633) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad; Aisha used to wake her family up on the twenty-third night."
"9634","(9634) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Yazid, he said: I saw Ibn Abbas sprinkled water on his family on the twenty-third night."
"9635","(9635) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Search for Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten days of Ramadan."
"9636","(9636) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Laylat al-Qadr is a night of turbidity, its sun rises but it has no rays."
"9637","(9637) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. When the last ten days came, he woke up his family and lifted the apron. It was said to Abu Bakr: Why did he lift the apron? He said: Women’s isolation."
"9638","(9638) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: He used to wake up his family in The last ten days."
"9639","(9639) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Sabit, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, he wakes up his family during the last ten days of Ramadan, and raises his hands during them."
"9640","(9640) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, who said: Abu Bakr used to pray. In Ramadan, like your prayers in the rest of the year, so when the ten days begin, be diligent."
"9641","(9641) Affan told us, he said: Abdul-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah told us, he said: He told us Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to strive diligently during the ten days. He does not strive for anything else."
"9642","(9642) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, and Abu Misra, who said: A man came to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Messenger of God, is there a man who fasts forever? He said: He neither fasted nor broke his fast."
"9643","(9643) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, and Sufyan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abu Abbas al-Makki, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He who fasts will not fast forever. (Bukhari 1979 and Muslim 187)"
"9644","(9644) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mahdi bin Maimun, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jarir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ma’bad al-Zamani, On the authority of Abu Qatada, he said: A man said: O Messenger of God, have you seen a man who fasts all his life? He said: He neither fasted nor broke his fast, or he neither fasted nor broke his fast. (Muslim 818, Abu Dawud 2418)"
"9645","(9645) Ubaid bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, on the authority of his father He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever fasts forever has neither fasted nor broken his fast. (Ibn Majah 1705. Tayalisi 1147)"
"9646","(9646) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Tamim al-Hajmi, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: Whoever fasts forever, Hell will be narrow for him, and he will be covered with his palm."
"9647","(9647) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak ibn Yasar, he heard it from Abu Tamimah, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, likewise. (Ahmad 4/414, Ibn Hibban 3584)"
"9648","(9648) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ammar Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, who said: A man said: Messenger of God, have you seen a man who fasts all his life? He said: I wish that he would not taste the whole of eternity. He said: Two-thirds of it? He said: More. He said: Half of it? He said: More, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Shall I not inform you of what will remove the heat of the chest: fasting for three days. Days of every month."
"9649","(9649) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khalid, on the authority of Abu Amr al-Shaybani, who said: It has reached Omar that a man fasts all the time. So he attached it to the pearl and started saying: Eat, ya dhar, eat, ya dhar."
"9650","(9650) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, who said: It was mentioned to Al-Sha’bi that the servant of the mukhtab fasted. All of eternity, he thought of that."
"9651","(9651) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Yazid, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; He was asked about daily fasting? His thoughts"
"9652","(9652) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, who said: Salim, Al-Qasim, and Ubaidullah were not there. They fast forever."
"9653","(9653) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Fara’i, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, who said: The Prophet of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: He who fasts forever will not fast."
"9654","(9654) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam; The black man used to fast all the time."
"9655","(9655) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid, who said: Urwa used to fast permanently while traveling and other than that."
"9656","(9656) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Abdullah bin Rahimah, on the authority of his grandmother, who said: Othman was He fasts all the time and stays awake all night except that he is hungry from the beginning."
"9657","(9657) Abd Allah and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Omar began fasting two years before his death."
"9658","(9658) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, who said: They mentioned seeing the crescent in Medina and said: The people of Istara saw him, so Al-Qasim and Salem said: What do we have to do with the people of Istara?"
"9659","(9659) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, spends the night at his side, and Bilal comes to him and gives him the call to prayer, and he gets up and takes a bath, so look at the Water came from his head, then it came out and I heard his voice during the Fajr prayer, then he continued fasting. Mutarrif said: So I said to Aamir: In Ramadan? He said: Yes, whether Ramadan or anything else. (Ahmad 6/254, Ibn Hibban 3490)"
"9660","(9660) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham. On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up in a state of ritual impurity, then take a bath, then complete his fast. (Bukhari 1925. Tirmidhi 779)"
"9661","(9661) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wake up in a state of ritual impurity, then he would take a bath, then he would come out of his bathtub and pray. people, and fast that day. (Nasa’i 2981, Ahmad 6/203)"
"9662","(9662) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Usama ibn Zayd, on the authority of Suleiman ibn Yasar, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: The Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He is junub without a wet dream, then he takes a bath and continues his fast. (Muslim 80. Ahmad 6/306)"
"9663","(9663) Abdi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Arak bin Malik, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Bakr; Umm Salama, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: If the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to He was junub without a wet dream, then he fasted in the morning. (Ahmad 6/313, Ibn Hibban 3486)"
"9664","(9664) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Jami’ ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Hilal, who said: Abdullah ibn Mirdas went to Abdullah bin Masoud, and he said: I was in a state of ritual impurity in the morning, so should I complete my fast? Abdullah said: In the morning, prayer is permissible for you, and fasting is permissible for you. Take a bath and complete your fast."
"9665","(9665) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Atiyya Al-Wadi’i, who said: Two men confronted each other. In the mosque there was a man in the morning while he was junub, so they went to Abdullah, and she went with them, and one of them asked him, and he said: Should he fast? He said: Yes, he said: So if he is one of the women? He said: Even if he was one of the women. He said: Even if he fell asleep intentionally? He said: Even if he fell asleep intentionally."
"9666","(9666) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Atiyya, on the authority of Abdullah; In a similar way"
"9667","(9667) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: If a man wakes up while he is junub and wants If he fasts, let him fast if he wishes."
"9668","(9668) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Ammar, a client of Banu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Zaid Ibn Thabit and Ibn Abbas; Concerning a man who wakes up in the morning while he is junub, they said: He continues his fast."
"9669","(9669) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abdullah, he said: Abu Dharr said: If I had been with my wife in the morning, I would have kept silent."
"9670","(9670) Shababi bin Siwar told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith bin Hisham, he said: Aisha and Umm Salamah told me; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to approach dawn while he was in the company of his family, then he would wash and fast. (Bukhari 1931. Tirmidhi 779)"
"9671","(9671) Shababā told us, he said: Hisham bin al-Ghaz told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: If the herald called and I I touched between her legs and completed the fast, whether it was Ramadan or something else."
"9672","(9672) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is sufficient for voluntary prayers, and it is fulfilled for obligatory prayers."
"9673","(9673) Aidh bin Habib told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: He is obligated to make up the judiciary."
"9674","(9674) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab; That Abu Hurairah retracted his fatwa; Whoever becomes junub in the morning has no fasting."
"9675","(9675) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Nafi’ narrated to us, saying: I heard Ibn Tawus mentioning, On the authority of Tawus, he said: If impurity befalls him during the month of Ramadan, then if he wakes up and does not wash himself until morning, then he will complete it. That day, and he fasts another day in its place. If he does not wake up, he does not have to do anything instead."
"9676","(9676) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, and Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Abdullah said: If the muezzin had given the call to prayer and I Between my wife's feet, I washed and then fasted."
"9677","(9677) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Omar said: If the call had reached me while I was between her feet I fasted, or he said: I did not break my fast."
"9678","(9678) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, continued, and we continued. This was reported to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: If the month were to extend it for me, I would continue in a way that those who are profound will abandon their deepening. I am not like you. I keep being fed and given to drink by my Lord. (Bukhari 1961, Tirmidhi 778)"
"9679","(9679) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, continued The people, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard that and they continued. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard that and he forbade them and said: I am not Like you, I stay with my Lord and He feeds me and gives me water. (Bukhari 1945, Muslim 775)"
"9680","(9680) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Ubaid Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, continued Ramadan, and the people continued it, but he forbade them, and it was said to him: Will you continue it? He said: I am not like you. I feed and give you drink. (Muslim 56. Ahmad 2/143)"
"9681","(9681) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salama, on the authority of Bishr ibn Harb, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, who said: I heard him say: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade keeping ties with each other, and this is my sister, she continues, and I forbid her. (Bukhari 1963 and Abu Dawud 2353)"
"9682","(9682) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-Ala, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Ali; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, continued until dawn. (Tabarani 1851, Ahmad 1/91)"
"9683","(9683) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of the Prophet’s companions May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. They said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, only forbade continuation of fasting and cupping for the fasting person. To spare his companions."
"9684","(9684) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Abu Qalabab; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade them from communicating with each other, so they said: O Messenger of God, are you communicating with each other? He said: I am not like you. I refused to have my Lord feed me and give me water. If I refuse, then from dawn to dawn."
"9685","(9685) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the continuity of fasting, so they said: Are you communicating? He said: I am not like you. I refused to let my Lord feed me and give me drink, or something like that."
"9686","(9686) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Huraira said: I will never continue."
"9687","(9687) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Janab, on the authority of Ismail ibn Raja’i, on the authority of Al-Nazzal ibn Sabra, on the authority of Ali, who said: No. And he prayed while fasting."
"9688","(9688) Ibn Fadil told us, on the authority of Amara ibn al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard it. He says: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Beware of upholding ties three times, so they said: You will continue to communicate, O Messenger of God. He said: In this regard, you are not like me. I refuse to have my Lord feed me and give me water, so perform as many deeds as you can bear.\n(Bukhari 1966. Ahmad 2/231)"
"9689","(9689) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Qadamī, he said: Aisha said: (Then complete the fast until the night) What it means is that she disliked communicating with each other."
"9690","(9690) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah; He said regarding the connection with fasting: God, Blessed and Most High, said: (Then complete the fast until the night), so when the night comes So he breaks the fast, then if he wishes he may fast, and if he wishes he may leave it."
"9691","(9691) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Bukair bin Amir, who said: Ibn Abi Na’am was wasil of fifteen years. One day until we return."
"9692","(9692) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Shayban, on the authority of Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab, who said: I entered upon Ibn Al-Zubayr is the fifteenth morning of the month, and he continues."
"9693","(9693) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khalid, he said: Muhammad bin Saad narrated to me, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck the other with one hand, then said: The month is like this and like this, then he decreased the third. A finger (Muslim 764. Ahmad 1/184)"
"9694","(9694) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Salmah ibn Kuhayl, on the authority of a man from Banu Sulaym, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, On the authority of Omar, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, isolated himself from his wives for a month, and when twenty-nine had passed, Gabriel came to him and said: The month has been fulfilled, and you have been justified."
"9695","(9695) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: How many months have passed? We said: Twenty-two days have passed, and eight remain. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Rather, twenty-two days have passed. And there remained seven days. They sought them out during the night, then he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The month is like this, and the month is like this. Like this, three times, and he stopped once. (Ahmad 2/251, Ibn Hibban 3450)"
"9696","(9696) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, swore May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, or he swore an oath for the month, so he ascended to him, and when it was twenty-nine days, Gabriel came to him and said: Come down, for the month has been completed."
"9697","(9697) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Qays, who said: I heard Sa’id ibn Amr narrating that he heard Ibn Omar narrated on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: We are an unlettered nation. We neither write nor count. The month is like this. And such and such, and such and such, and holding the thumb on the third? And the month is like this, and like this, and like this, meaning: the completion of the thirty days. (Bukhari 1913, Muslim 761)"
"9698","(9698) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The month is like this, and like this, and like that, then he decreased his thumb, meaning: nine. And twenty (Muslim 7591 Abu Dawud 2314)"
"9699","(9699) Yazeed bin Harun told us, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had one of his wives for a month, so he sat in a drinking room for him, then he came down on the twenty-nine. They said: O Messenger of God, have you visited this month? He said: The month is twenty-nine. (Bukhari 1911)"
"9700","(9700) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, on the authority of Sa’id bin Amr, that Abdullah bin Omar He told them that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: We are an unlettered nation. We neither write nor count. The month is like this. And so on, and he struck three times with his hand, then subtracted one. (Ahmad 2/129)"
"9701","(9701) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdul Rahman bin Hatib, on the authority of Ibn Omar He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The month is twenty-nine, then he applied the kafa’ twice, and applied the third. He held out his thumb, and Aisha said: May God forgive Abu Abdul Rahman, but the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, abandoned his wives. A month, so he descended for the twenty-nine, and they said: O Messenger of God, have you had a month? He said: And the month will be twenty-nine. (Ahmad 2/31)"
"9702","(9702) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of Husayn bin Qubaysiyya, on the authority of Ali, he said : The twenty-nineth month, and the thirty-ninth month."
"9703","(9703) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Yazid, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafli, who said: I heard Omar say: The months; Thirty-nine months, twenty-nine months."
"9704","(9704) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Musab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Ramadan is the ninth day. And twenty."
"9705","(9705) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Aynah, who said: We fasted Ramadan during the reign of Ali. Other than his vision, twenty-eight days, so when it was the Day of Fitr, he commanded us to make up for a day."
"9706","(9706) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: We did not fast the twenty-nine days, more than We fasted for thirty days."
"9707","(9707) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Yazid bin Hulayl, who said: When a fasting person eats food, his joints feel blessed."
"9708","(9708) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Habib ibn Zaid, on the authority of a woman called: Layla, on the authority of Umm Amara, she said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us and food was brought to him, and some of those with him were fasting, so the Prophet said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: When a fasting person eats food, the angels bless him. (Tirmidhi 786. Ahmad 6/365)"
"9709","(9709) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail bin Sa’im, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: When a fasting person eats, he praises him. joints"
"9710","(9710) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The fasting person when... He ate there, and the angels prayed for him."
"9711","(9711) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Abi Fakhita, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Al-Mu’tikaf Ali Fasting"
"9712","(9712) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: There is no i’tikaf except by fasting."
"9713","(9713) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas and Aisha, who said: There is no i’tikaf except By fasting, and Ali and Ibn Masoud said: He does not have to fast, unless he imposes it on himself."
"9714","(9714) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no i’tikaf. Except by fasting"
"9715","(9715) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha; In the same way"
"9716","(9716) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali and Abdullah, who said: The one who secludes himself is not upon him. Fasting, unless he stipulates that for himself."
"9717","(9717) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Fasting is obligatory for him."
"9718","(9718) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, who said: There is no i’tikaf except by fasting."
"9719","(9719) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is not seen as i’tikaf except with fasting."
"9720","(9720) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: He said: Ali: The one who is in seclusion must fast, even if he does not impose it on himself."
"9721","(9721) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He is not obligated to fast, except That he made it obligatory for himself."
"9722","(9722) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Like the saying of Abraham."
"9723","(9723) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is no i’tikaf except with fasting."
"9724","(9724) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: If a man secludes Let the congregation witness, let him visit the sick, let him attend the funeral, let his family come, let him command them to perform the Hajj, and he Standing"
"9725","(9725) Hushaym told us, he said: Al-Shaybani told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, that he said: The congregation shall bear witness, The sick person returns and responds to the imam."
"9726","(9726) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Amr told us, on the authority of Aisha; She would not visit a sick person with her family while she was in seclusion, unless she passed away."
"9727","(9727) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: He performs the congregation’s witness, and returns. The sick person, and he attends the funeral, and goes out to the pilgrim, and responds to the imam, and that is because Amr bin Harith was sent to him While he was in seclusion, he did not come to him, so he sent for him and he came to him."
"9728","(9728) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to like the person in seclusion to stipulate These qualities are his, even if he does not stipulate; To attend the sick person, to follow the funeral procession, and to witness the congregation."
"9729","(9729) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He goes out to the toilet, and the sick person returns, and comes Friday, and he stands at the door."
"9730","(9730) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The congregation will come."
"9731","(9731) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salama, who said: The one who is in seclusion returns. He is sick, and he witnesses the gathering, and he stands with the man on the road and asks him."
"9732","(9732) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He comes to defecate, follows the funeral, and returns. The patient"
"9733","(9733) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: The congregation will testify, and the sick person will return. He will attend the funeral. He once said: He will answer the imam."
"9734","(9734) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Sufyan bin Hussein told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, She said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in seclusion, he would not enter the house, except for a need. (Bukhari 2029. Ahmad 6/235)"
"9735","(9735) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha; She used to pass by a sick family member while she was in seclusion, so she would not approach him."
"9736","(9736) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab (h) and on the authority of Sufyan On the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, they said: The one who is in seclusion does not attend a funeral, nor does he visit one who is sick."
"9737","(9737) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: He does not follow a funeral procession, nor visit a sick person, nor respond to prayers. Invitation"
"9738","(9738) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The one who is in seclusion does not follow a funeral procession, nor does he He returns ill."
"9739","(9739) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: He does not answer a supplication, nor does he visit a sick person, nor does he attend. funeral"
"9740","(9740) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Amriya, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, if he wanted to seclude himself, he would pray the morning prayer, then he would enter the place where he would seclude himself. (Muslim 831. Abu Dawud 2456)"
"9741","(9741) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man wants to seclude himself, let the sun set for him. The night he wanted to seclude himself in the mosque."
"9742","(9742) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; Regarding the person who is in seclusion, he stipulates that he should seclude during the day and come to his family at night. He said: This is not seclusion."
"9743","(9743) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroubah, on the authority of his leaders; He did not see any harm in a person in seclusion stipulating that he should have dinner with his family and perform the suhoor meal."
"9744","(9744) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he wishes, he stipulates that he may have dinner with his family. He does not enter his shade, but his dinner is brought in the courtyard of his house."
"9745","(9745) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ya’la ibn Umayyah; He used to say to his companion: Go with us to the mosque, and we will seclude ourselves there for an hour."
"9746","(9746) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Whenever Ibn Umar wanted to seclude He went to a tent, or a tent, and fulfilled his need therein, but did not come to his family, nor did he enter a roof."
"9747","(9747) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Alaqah, on the authority of his paternal uncle Qutba ibn Malik; Omar saw people secluding themselves in the mosque, and they were covered, so he disapproved of it, and said: What is this? They said: We only cover our food. He said: So cover it, so if you are fed, eat it."
"9748","(9748) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The one who is in seclusion does not enter a roofed house."
"9749","(9749) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He does not enter a ceiling."
"9750","(9750) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salama, who said: He does not enter a house."
"9751","(9751) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He should not enter a house."
"9752","(9752) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He should not enter a house."
"9753","(9753) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub; That Abu Qulabab secluded himself in the mosque of his people."
"9754","(9754) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Khaled; That Abu Qulaab did it."
"9755","(9755) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; He secluded himself in the mosque of his people."
"9756","(9756) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; He secluded himself in the mosque of his people."
"9757","(9757) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammam bin Al-Harith; He secluded himself in the mosque of his people."
"9758","(9758) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in seclusion in mosques. Tribes"
"9759","(9759) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salama; He saw no harm in secluding himself in a mosque and praying there."
"9760","(9760) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Za’ara’; That Abu Al-Ahwas secluded himself in the mosque of his people."
"9761","(9761) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: If he wishes, he may seclude himself in the mosque of his people."
"9762","(9762) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil al-Ahdab, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Hudhayfy came to Abdullah, He said: Don't you like the people of Aquf, between your house and the house of Al-Ash'ari, meaning: the mosque? Abdullah said: Perhaps they were right and I was wrong. Hudhayfy said: Didn’t you know that there is no i’tikaf except in three mosques? The Sacred Mosque, and the Al-Aqsa Mosque, and the Mosque of the Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I do not care whether I seclude in it, or in This is your market."
"9763","(9763) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali (h) and on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Sa’d bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ali, who said: There is no i’tikaf except in a comprehensive Egypt."
"9764","(9764) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Aqmar, on the authority of Shaddad ibn al-Azma’, who said: A man secluded himself in The greatest mosque, and he set up tents, and the people surrounded him. This reached Ibn Masoud, so he sent a man to him, so the people stopped him. And that was good."
"9765","(9765) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: There is no i’tikaf except in a mosque. Prophet"
"9766","(9766) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There is no i’tikaf except in a mosque where the congregation gathers."
"9767","(9767) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about itikaf? They said: Do not seclude except in a mosque where they gather together."
"9768","(9768) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: There is no seclusion except in a mosque in which the congregation is gathered."
"9769","(9769) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: There is no i’tikaf except in a congregational mosque."
"9770","(9770) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalab; He was brought to the mosque of his people on the Day of Fitr, and he secluded himself there with decorated robes, and he made them sit in his lap. Then he embraced her and went out to the prayer hall as he was from the mosque."
"9771","(9771) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to prefer it. The one who is in seclusion may spend the night of Fitr in his mosque, until his morning comes there."
"9772","(9772) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: He spent the night of Fitr in the mosque in which I secluded myself. Therein, until your morning comes to your place of prayer."
"9773","(9773) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If he has intercourse The one who is in seclusion, he annulled his itikaf and resumed it."
"9774","(9774) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He makes up for his itikaf."
"9775","(9775) Ibn al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Musa ibn Abi Ma’bad, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, al-Qasim, and Salem, they said: He receives."
"9776","(9776) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who cheated on his wife while he was in itikaf, he is in the same position as he who cheated in Ramadan. In Ramadan."
"9777","(9777) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamiya ibn Marthad, on the authority of Ad-Dahhak, he said: They used to have intercourse while they were They were secluded until the verse was revealed: {And do not associate with them while you are secluded in the mosques}"
"9778","(9778) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Whoever has sexual intercourse with his wife while he is in seclusion He is required to pay expiation like the one who is afflicted in Ramadan."
"9779","(9779) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of al-Shaybani, on the authority of Bukair ibn al-Akhnas, on the authority of Mujahid; In a person who is in i'tikaf, when he has intercourse, he says: He gives two dinars in charity."
"9780","(9780) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a woman who vowed to seclude herself for fifty days, so she remained secluded for forty, then her husband came and sent for her, so she went to him. He said: Complete what remains."
"9781","(9781) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata’, that he disliked for the one in seclusion to kiss, or Immediately"
"9782","(9782) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The one who is in i’tikaf does not kiss. And he does not communicate with you."
"9783","(9783) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The one who secludes himself neither sells nor He buys"
"9784","(9784) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ammar bin Abdullah bin Yassar, on the authority of his father; Ali helped Ja`d ibn Hubayra with seven hundred dirhams of his gift for the price of a servant of his, so he asked him: Have you bought a servant? ? He said: I am in seclusion. He said: What do you have to do if you go to the market and buy a servant?"
"9785","(9785) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Laith, who said: Tawoos was asked about a woman who died and she had to seclude herself. He spent a year in the Sacred Mosque, and she has four sons, all of whom would love to perform the prayer on her behalf? Tawus said: The four of you seclude yourself in the Sacred Mosque for three months and fast."
"9786","(9786) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, who said: It is not sufficient for the dead to perform i’tikaf."
"9787","(9787) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Abd Allah bin Reproach His mother vowed to seclude herself for ten days, but she died and did not seclude herself, so Ibn Abbas said: Abstain from your mother."
"9788","(9788) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Amer bin Musab; Aisha kept away from her brother after he died."
"9789","(9789) Hushaym bin Bashir narrated to us, saying: Hajjaj narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’; He did not see any harm in a secluded person washing his clothes or sewing them."
"9790","(9790) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, he said: Sufyan bin Hussein narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha. She said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in seclusion, he would not enter the house except for a need. She said: So I washed myself. His head, and indeed, between me and him is the threshold of the door. (Bukhari 2951 Abu Dawud 2461)"
"9791","(9791) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When a woman in itikaf is menstruating, she should cover herself in her home, and she Therein"
"9792","(9792) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, who said: Al-Mu’tikafah strikes its building at the door of the mosque when She menstruated."
"9793","(9793) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Ikrimah; Some of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, were menstruating while she was single."
"9794","(9794) Abbad told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated for the secluded person to enter the grave."
"9795","(9795) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Salem; He said: He prepared food and sent it to Saeed bin Jubayr, and he said: I am fasting, so he told him the hadith of Salman. He broke the fast with Abu Darda, so he broke the fast."
"9796","(9796) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Bura, on the authority of Kharshi ibn Al-Hurr, who said: We were with Omar and he brought food. So he said to the people: Eat, and they all said: I am fasting. So he decided for them to break the fast, so they broke the fast."
"9797","(9797) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Suleiman bin Musa asked him whether a man broke his fast. For his guest? He said: Yes."
"9798","(9798) Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; If a guest came to visit a fasting man, he would allow him to break his fast and spend the day in his place."
"9799","(9799) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who fasted voluntarily but his mother forbade him? They said: He obeys her and fasts sometimes."
"9800","(9800) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I told him: My mother swears that I will not pray again What is written is something, and I do not fast except an obligatory fast, out of pity for me? He said: I will justify her oath."
"9801","(9801) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: I asked an alcoholic person about a man who had become fasting in the morning, and then Did his mother tell him to break the fast? It is as if he disliked that and said: He will fast another day in its place."
"9802","(9802) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: She came The wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Prophet of God, what is the husband’s right over his wife? He said: Do not fast except with His permission, except the obligatory fast. If she does that, she has sinned, and it will not be accepted from her. (Abu Dawud 1951)"
"9803","(9803) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Zaid bin Wahhab, who said: Omar wrote to us that a woman should not fast. Voluntarily, except with her husband’s permission."
"9804","(9804) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Do not fast voluntarily while he is present. Except by His permission."
"9805","(9805) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Uthman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: A woman should not fast except with her husband’s permission. (Bukhari 51951 Muslim 84)"
"9806","(9806) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abi Al-Khalil, on the authority of Abi Qatada, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: A customary fast is an expiation for two years: a past year and a future year."
"9807","(9807) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mahdi bin Maimun, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jarir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ma’bad al-Zamani, On the authority of Abu Qatada: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about his customary fasting? He said: I consider God to be atonement for two years: a past year and a future year."
"9808","(9808) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Qais, on the authority of Huzayl, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha; She used to fast in Arafah."
"9809","(9809) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Qais, on the authority of Huzayl, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: There is no The Sunnah is a day I prefer to fast on than the Day of Arafah."
"9810","(9810) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Abu Hafs al-Taifi, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Saul bin Saad, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: A customary fast is an expiation for two years. (Abu Ali 7548. Tabarani 5923)"
"9811","(9811) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, that he used to fast in custom."
"9812","(9812) Ishaq Al-Azraq narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said regarding a customary fast. Hadra: If there is a difference of opinion, then he should not fast."
"9813","(9813) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: They did not consider fasting They knew it was a bad thing, unless they feared it would be the day of slaughter."
"9814","(9814) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Mujahid, that Aisha said: A customary fast Atonement for half a year. He said: And Mujahid said. So-and-so said: Atonement for a year."
"9815","(9815) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hamid al-Tawil told us, he said: It was mentioned by Al-Hasan that fasting was known to him. It is equivalent to fasting for a year. Al-Hasan said: I do not know of a day superior to a day, nor a night superior to a night, except for the night. Destiny, for it is better than a thousand months, and I saw Othman bin Abi Al-Aas fasting on the day of Arafah, sprinkling water on him. Treat him with it, and he will become cool with it."
"9816","(9816) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Saad bin Saeed, he said: I heard Omar bin Thabit, he said: I heard Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever fasts Ramadan, then follows it with six days of Shawwal, has He fasted for a lifetime, or as if he fasted for a lifetime. (Tirmidhi 759. Abu Dawud 2425)"
"9817","(9817) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: When he mentioned the six days that Some people voluntarily fast it after Ramadan. He said: He says: God Almighty has been pleased with this month for all of the years."
"9818","(9818) Hafs told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Aisha said: If I was obligated to fast during the month of Ramadan, so I would not fulfill it until Shaaban came. (Bukhari 1950, Muslim 151)"
"9819","(9819) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abdullah Al-Bayhi, on the authority of Aisha, who said: What I used to complete what remained of Ramadan during the lifetime of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except in Sha`ban. (Tirmidhi 783. Ahmad 6/179)"
"9820","(9820) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar narrated to us, saying: He who I do not trust narrated to me, on the authority of Ubadah ibn The silent one, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw the crescent, he would say: God is great, God is great, praise be to God, There is no power or strength except with God. Oh God, I ask you for the best of this month, and I seek refuge in you from the evil of destiny, and from the evil of Day of Judgment. (Darimi 1687, Ibn Hibban 888)"
"9821","(9821) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, who said: I left the mosque with Sa`id bin al-Musayyab. So we said: This is the Crescent, O Abu Muhammad. Then when he saw it, he said: I believe in Him who created you, and He formed you and made you equal. Then he turned to me and said: : Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw the crescent moon, he would say thus. (Abdul Razzaq 7351)"
"9822","(9822) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ubaid ibn Amr, on the authority of Ali, who said: When he saw One of you has the crescent, so do not raise his head with it. It is sufficient for one of you to say: My Lord and your Lord is God."
"9823","(9823) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When you see the crescent, say: My Lord and your Lord. God"
"9824","(9824) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, that Ali used to say when he saw the crescent: O God, grant us victory. By His goodness, His blessing, His victory, and His light, we seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what comes after it."
"9825","(9825) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of a man from al-Nakh`, on the authority of Abu Masoud al-Badri, who said: Because something else than this palace is more beloved to me than to do as they do. If one of you sees the crescent, it is as if he sees his Lord."
"9826","(9826) Hussein bin Ali told us, he said: I asked Hisham bin Hassan: What did Al-Hasan say when he saw the crescent moon? He said: He used to say: Oh God, make it a month of blessings, light, reward and well-being. Oh God, you are the divider among your servants. Good, so divide for us from it the best that you divide among your righteous servants."
"9827","(9827) Hussein bin Ali told us, he said: I asked Ibn Juraij, and he mentioned, about Ata’: that a man took the family of a slave from The earth, he said: Then he heard someone saying: Oh God, bestow upon us security and faith, peace and Islam, guidance and forgiveness. And success in what you are pleased with, and protection from what you are displeased with. My Lord and your Lord is God. He said: He continued meeting them until I preserved them, and I did not I see someone."
"9828","(9828) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to wonder when The man saw the Crescent to say: My Lord and your Lord is God."
"9829","(9829) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He hated it. Signaling when the crescent is sighted and raising the voice."
"9830","(9830) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders; When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a crescent, he would say: A crescent of goodness and guidance, a crescent of goodness and guidance. I believe. By the One who created you, three times: Praise be to God, who brought about such-and-such a month. (Abu Dawud 5051)"
"9831","(9831) Ali told us, he said: Hajjaj bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He hated to stand up for the crescents, but he would object and say: God is Great, and praise be to God who went with the crescents. Such and such, and he brought the crescent of such and such."
"9832","(9832) Abbad told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about Nowruz fasting? He thought of him and said: You will honor him."
"9833","(9833) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, he said: Al-Hasan was asked about fasting on the day of Nowruz? He said: What do you have to do with Nowruz? Do not pay attention to it, for it is only for non-Arabs."
"9834","(9834) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Numayr ibn Urayb, on the authority of Aamir ibn Masoud, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Fasting in the cold winter is a prey. (Ahmad 4/335 Tirmidhi 797)"
"9835","(9835) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: Omar said: winter. The spoils of the worshiper."
"9836","(9836) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, he said: He used to say when winter came: O people of the Qur’an, the night is long for your prayers, and the day is short for your fasting, so take advantage."
"9837","(9837) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Zuhara, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to He fasted, then broke his fast. He said: Oh God, I fasted for you and for your provision I broke my fast. He said: Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym used to say: Praise be to God. He who helped me, so I fasted, and provided for me, so I broke my fast. (Abu Dawud 2349. An-Nasa’i 10131)"
"9838","(9838) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, when he broke his fast with a family, he said: May the fasting people break their fast with you and the righteous eat your food. And the verse was revealed. May the angels be upon you. (Ahmad 3/118, Darmi 1772)"
"9839","(9839) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Thabit bin Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Awf bin Malik Al-Ashja’i, who said: Omar said: Fasting a day other than Ramadan and feeding a poor person is equivalent to fasting a day other than Ramadan."
"9840","(9840) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast during the month until we say: He does not break his fast, and he would break his fast until we say: He does not break the fast. He fasts some of it. (Muslim 1800, Tirmidhi 769)"
"9841","(9841) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Othman bin Hakim told us, he said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about fasting in Rajab? He said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast to the point that we say: He does not break his fast, and he broke his fast. We even say: He does not fast. (Bukhari 1971, Muslim 178)"
"9842","(9842) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Qatadā, on the authority of Zurārah ibn Awfa, on the authority of Saad ibn Hisham, On the authority of Aisha, who said: I do not know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ever fasted a full month, except Ramadan. (Abu Dawud 1339, Muslim 139)"
"9843","(9843) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, he said: I asked her about fasting. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: I have never known him to fast a month until he breaks his fast during it, except Ramadan, and I will not break his fast until he breaks his fast during it. (Muslim 8091, Ahmad 6/157)"
"9844","(9844) Yahya bin Sulaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Kathir, on the authority of Asim bin Laqit bin Sabrah, on the authority of His father, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Exaggerate the inhalation, unless you are fasting."
"9845","(9845) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of his father, who said: Al-Dahhak and his companions were in Khurasan during Ramadan, and they were not They rinse their mouths."
"9846","(9846) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: He hated to inhale The fasting person so that it does not enter his throat."
"9847","(9847) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Ammar bin Ruzaiq, on the authority of Abu Farwa, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, he said: If you inhale While you are fasting, do not exaggerate."
"9848","(9848) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abis, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: If one of you is fasting, let him wipe it so that no traces of his fast can be seen on him, and if he spits He covered his slug, and Yazid gestured with his hand as if he was covering his mouth with it."
"9849","(9849) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yassaf, who said: Issa ibn Maryam said: If the day If any of you fasts, let him cleanse his lips."
"9850","(9850) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Then You started fasting in the morning, so they became mad."
"9851","(9851) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Bura ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Kharshi ibn al-Hurr, who said: I saw Omar He strikes the palms of the people in Rajab until they place them in the palm of their hands and says: Eat, for it is only a month that he used to venerate. People of pre-Islamic times"
"9852","(9852) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about Fasting in Rajab? He said: Where are you from Sha`ban? (Abdul Razzaq 7858)"
"9853","(9853) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid, the servant of the Saba’i, on the authority of a man who named him, on the authority of Anas, who said: Do not Monday, Thursday, or rugby."
"9854","(9854) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Muhammad, on the authority of his father, who said: Ibn Umar used to see people not preparing for Rajab. He hated that."
"9855","(9855) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: I asked Aisha about The fasting of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: He used to fast to the point that we said: He does not break the fast, and he broke the fast to the point that we say: He does not fast, and I have never seen him fast more in any month. In Sha`ban, he used to fast all of Sha`ban except for a little while. Rather, he used to fast all of Sha`ban. (Bukhari 1919, Abu Dawud 2426)"
"9856","(9856) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Sadiqah bin Musa told us, he said: Thabit al-Bunani told us, on the authority of Anas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the best fasting? He said: Fasting in Sha`ban is to honor Ramadan. (Tirmidhi 663, Abu Ali 3431)"
"9857","(9857) Yazeed told us, he said: Al-Mas’udi told us, on the authority of Al-Muhajir Abi Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, he said: Why The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast more frequently than he did in Sha`ban, and that is because it is abrogated in it. The deadlines for someone who dies in a year."
"9858","(9858) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Thabit ibn Qays narrated to me, he said: Abu Sa’id al-Maqbari narrated to me, he said: Abu Hurairah narrated to me, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, I saw you fasting in Sha`ban, not a fast. Do you fast during any of the months, except during the month of Ramadan? He said: That is a month that people ignore, between Rajab and the month of Ramadan, in which people’s deeds are taken up, so I would like it not to be taken up. I have nothing to do except when I am fasting. (Ahmed 5/201)"
"9859","(9859) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Labid, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, he said: I asked her About the fasting of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: I have never seen him fast in any month more than he fasted in Sha`ban. He used to fast all of Sha`ban. He used to fast Sha`ban except a little while. (Muslim 1761, Ibn Majah 1710)"
"9860","(9860) Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Ubaid, the client of Ibn Azhar, who said: I witnessed the Eid with Omar bin Al-Khattab, so he began with the prayer before the sermon, and said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the fasting of these people. The two days: As for the Day of Fitr, it is the day you break your fast, and as for the Day of Sacrifice, eat meat on it. Your rituals (Bukhari 5573, Tirmidhi 771)"
"9861","(9861) Ibn Numayr and Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Saad bin Sa’id, who said: Amr bint Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade fasting on the Day of Fitr and the Day of Sacrifice. (Muslim 143)"
"9862","(9862) Yahya bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Qaz’a, on the authority of Abu Sa’id; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade fasting on the Day of Fitr and the Day of Sacrifice. (Bukhari 1995, Tirmidhi 799)"
"9863","(9863) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The Day of Arafah, the Day of Sacrifice, and the Days of Tashreeq, days of eating and drinking. (Tirmidhi 773, Abu Dawud 2411)"
"9864","(9864) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Jubayr, who said: A man came to Ibn Umar and asked him about a man. He vowed to fast one day, so he broke his fast, or did he sacrifice? He said: God Almighty commanded the fulfillment of the vow, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade fasting on this day. (Bukhari 1994, Muslim 800)"
"9865","(9865) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him regarding the breaking of the fast and the day of sacrifice. (Bukhari 6705)"
"9866","(9866) Ibn Numayr and Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Utba, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade fasting on the day of Al-Fitr and the Day of Sacrifice. (Bukhari 1991, Muslim 141)"
"9867","(9867) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abi Wada’i, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, He said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I broke my fast one day of Ramadan, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Give alms, ask God for forgiveness, and fast a day in its place. (Abu Dawud 2385. Darqutni 27)"
"9868","(9868) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha’, he said: Asim said to me: I asked Jabir bin Zayd: What has reached you regarding whom? If he breaks the fast on a day of Ramadan, what does he have to do? He said: Let him fast a day in his place, and do a good deed with that."
"9869","(9869) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, they said: He makes up for a day. His place"
"9870","(9870) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: He will be in his place one day."
"9871","(9871) Abdi told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Ali bin Hakim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; Concerning a man who intentionally broke his fast one day in Ramadan, he said: He asks God for forgiveness for that and repents to Him, and makes up the day. His place"
"9872","(9872) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of Sa`id, the same."
"9873","(9873) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, who said: Abu Qalābāb sent to Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab to ask him about a man who broke his fast. One day of Ramadan intentionally? Saeed said: He fasts in place of every day he breaks his fast during the month."
"9874","(9874) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab; Regarding a man who breaks his fast one day of Ramadan intentionally, he said: He is fasting for a month."
"9875","(9875) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He must fast for three thousand days."
"9876","(9876) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ibn al-Mutawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Huraira, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever breaks the fast on a day without making a concession will not be rewarded. Fasting forever. (Ibn Majah 1472. Ahmad 2/442)"
"9877","(9877) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Mughiriya al-Yashkari, on the authority of So-and-so ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Masoud said: Whoever breaks his fast on a day of Ramadan without a concession, he will not be rewarded by fasting for the whole life. (Abdul Razzaq 7476)"
"9878","(9878) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Ali, on the authority of Arfaja, on the authority of Ali, who said: Whoever breaks his fast on the day of He made up Ramadan intentionally and never made it up for the rest of his life."
"9879","(9879) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: A man came to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: You were destroyed. He said: What destroyed you? He said: I had intercourse with my wife during Ramadan. He said: Free a slave. He said: I do not think so. He said: Fast for two months. He said: I cannot. He said: Feed sixty poor people. He said: I cannot find it. He said: Sit. So he sat. While he was like that, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came. May God bless him and grant him peace, with an arak containing dates. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Go and give it in charity. He said: By the one He has sent you with the truth. There is no woman among her family who is poorer than us. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed at you. Until his fangs showed, then he said: Go, and feed your children with it. (Bukhari 67111 Muslim 81)"
"9880","(9880) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Fast a day in its place. (Ahmed 2/208)"
"9881","(9881) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jafar bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came A man greeted him and mentioned that he had been burned, so he asked him about his situation, and he mentioned that he had intercourse with his wife during Ramadan, so he came to the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, with a lump called arak, which contains dates. He said: Where is the burnt one? So the man got up and said to him: Give this in charity. (Bukhari 6822 and Abu Dawud 2386)"
"9882","(9882) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not pray until he broke his fast, even by drinking water. (Ibn Hibban 3504, Abu Ali 3780)"
"9883","(9883) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Hakim, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Abu Barza Al-Aslami, he said: He was commanding People should break their fast before the prayer as much as possible."
"9884","(9884) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The black man would not break his fast in Ramadan until he had prayed. Morocco"
"9885","(9885) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman; Omar and Othman used to pray the Maghrib prayer when they saw night, and they used to break their fast before they prayed."
"9886","(9886) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning a man whose throat flies enter, he said: It does not break the fast."
"9887","(9887) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: It does not break the fast."
"9888","(9888) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It does not break the fast."
"9889","(9889) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Hafsa bint Sirin, on the authority of Al-Rabbab, on the authority of her paternal uncle Salman bin Amir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you breaks his fast, let him break his fast with dates, and if he does not find anything, let him break his fast with water. For it is pure. (Tirmidhi 658 and Ibn Majah 1699)"
"9890","(9890) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Hafsa bint Sirin, on the authority of Al-Rubaab, and she is the mother of the scent, the daughter of Salla’, on the authority of Salman bin Amer, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you breaks the fast, let him break his fast with dates. If he does not find it, let him break his fast with water, for it is pure. (Tirmidhi 658. Ahmad 4/17)"
"9891","(9891) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: I entered upon him. So he broke his fast with dates."
"9892","(9892) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Umm Musa, who said: They liked to break the fast in peace, or Dates"
"9893","(9893) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Mughirah bin Abdullah Al-Shakri, who said: Abdullah said: Who If he deliberately breaks the fast on a day of Ramadan without travel or illness, he will not make it up at all, even if he fasts for the whole life."
"9894","(9894) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He will spend one day in his place and ask for forgiveness. Lord"
"9895","(9895) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Hilal al-Absi, on the authority of Jarir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us and urged us to be honest, but they delayed until anger was seen on his face. Then... A man from the Ansar came with a basket and gave it to her. The people followed until happiness was seen on his face. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever enacts a good Sunnah will have its reward, and a similar reward to whoever acts according to it, without detracting from it. Their wages are nothing, and whoever does an evil practice will bear its burden, and the burden of whoever acts upon it, without detracting from it. Their burdens are nothing."
"9896","(9896) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, he said: Aoun bin Abi Juhaif told me, he said: I heard Al-Mundhir bin Jarir. It is mentioned, on the authority of his father, that he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the beginning of the day. He said: Then a barefoot people came to him. Mujtabī al-Nimār, on them are swords and turbans, some of them are from Mudar, nay, all of them are from Mudar. He said: Then I saw the face of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he changed greatly because of the immorality he saw in them. He said: Then he got up and entered the mosque, then he ordered Bilal So he gave the call to prayer, then he stood and prayed, then he said: {O people, fear your Lord, who created you from a single soul}, then he recited to another. Verses: {And fear Allah by whom you question, and the relatives}, {Fear Allah and let a soul see what it has put forward for the morrow} A person gives in charity from a dinar. And from his dirhams, and from his clothes, and from a saa of wheat, meaning wheat, and from a saa of dates until he said: even if it were half a date, he said: Then a man from the Ansar came with a vision that was almost incapable of being able to handle it, in fact it was unable to handle it. He said: Then the people followed one another until they saw Heaps of food and clothes. He said: I saw the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rejoicing, as if He is a madhhab, and he said: Whoever establishes a good practice in Islam, or does righteous deeds, and follows it well after him, will have its reward and a reward. Whoever does it after him, it will not detract from their rewards in the slightest, and whoever follows a bad tradition in Islam, his followers will follow it, It was his burden and the burden of whoever did it after him, without any of their burdens being diminished. (Muslim 7060 Ahmad 4/359)"
"9897","(9897) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I heard Ata’, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I bear witness to the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed before the sermon, then he delivered the sermon, and he saw that he did not listen to the women, so he came to them. So he reminded them, and admonished them, and commanded them to be truthful, and Bilal, wearing his garment, said: Then the woman began to throw the ring. And the khuras and the thing."
"9898","(9898) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Mahan, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Give charity, O women, for you are the majority of the people of Hell. A woman who is not one of the women said: Aliyah an-Nasa’: What is that about, O Messenger of God? He said: Because you curse a lot and disbelieve your family. (Ahmad 1/376, Tayalisi 384)"
"9899","(9899) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murr, on the authority of Khaythami, on the authority of Adiy ibn Hatim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, mentioned the Fire, so he turned his face away and veiled himself, then he mentioned the Fire, so he turned away and veiled himself, until We thought it was as if he was looking at it, then he said: Fear the Fire, even if only half a date, and whoever does not find it, then speak to him. good (Bukhari 6540 and Muslim 68)"
"9900","(9900) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Maqil, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Fear the Fire, even if it is half a date. (Bukhari 1417, Muslim 703)"
"9901","(9901) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Dawud bin Qays narrated to us, saying: Iyad bin Abdullah bin Saad bin Abi Sarh narrated to us. On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to go out on the day of Eid, the day of breaking the fast. So he leads the people in prayer with the same two rak'ahs, then he says the salutation, then he gets up and faces the people while they are sitting and says: Give charity. They gave in charity: Most of the women gave in charity in earrings, rings and other things. (Bukhari 1462, Muslim 605)"
"9902","(9902) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Amr ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Zainab, the wife of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to give charity, and he said: Give charity, O women. (Bukhari 1466, Tirmidhi 636)"
"9903","(9903) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Mansour ibn Hayyan, on the authority of Ibn Bijad, on the authority of his grandmother, she said: I said: O Messenger By God, the beggar has come to me. I have nothing to give him. She said: He said: Do not repel your beggar except with anything, even if it is unjustly. (Bukhari 845. Tabarani 561)"
"9904","(9904) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ma’bad bin Khalid, on the authority of Harithah bin Wahb Al-Khuza’i, who said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Give charity, for a man is about to go out with his charity and there will be no one to accept it. (Bukhari 1411, Muslim 700)"
"9905","(9905) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Rashid ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: What is on the earth of Sadaqah will come out until the beards of seventy devils are freed from it, all of them forbidding it. (Ibn Khuzaymah 2457, Hakim 417)"
"9906","(9906) Omar bin Saad told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abu Al-Za’ari, on the authority of Abdullah; That Rabi Abdullah had fasted for sixty years, and a woman came and descended beside him. He descended to her and had intercourse with her for six years. for several nights, then it was dropped into his hands, then he escaped, so he went to a mosque and took shelter in it, and he stayed for three days without eating anything, so he came With a loaf of bread, he broke half of it and gave it to one man on his right, and he gave it to another on his left. Then an angel was sent to him. Then his soul was taken, and the work of sixty years was placed on one palm, and the bad deeds were placed on the other, and it outweighed, then the loaf was brought."
"9907","(9907) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he says: God accepts charity, and He takes it with His right hand and raises it for its owner. Just as one of you raises his foal, or his offspring, to the point that a morsel becomes like a human body, and this is confirmed in the Book of God. Almighty and Majestic: {It is He who accepts repentance from His servants and takes alms}, and {Allah eliminates usury and raises alms}"
"9908","(9908) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Yunus ibn Khabab, on the authority of Abu Salama, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Your wealth is never lacking in charity, so give in charity. (Ahmad 1/1931 Abu Ali 845)"
"9909","(9909) Yahya bin Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was given to us. A grilled sheep, so I divided it all except its two shoulders, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me and I mentioned that. He said: No, it is all yours except his shoulders. (Tirmidhi 2470, Ahmad 6/50)"
"9910","(9910) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Atiyya, the client of Banu Amir, on the authority of Yazid bin Bishr. Al-Sakskiy, he said: He sent Zayd ibn Abd al-Malik with a cloth to the Kaaba, and when he came to Taima’, a beggar came to him and asked He said: So he said: Give charity, for charity saves you from seventy types of evil. He said: So I said: Who among us is wise? They said: He forgot, a man from among the Jews. So I came to the house and said: Then he forgot? So his wife looked over at me and gave me permission, so I entered upon him. When he saw me, he performed ablution, and I said to him: What happened to you when you saw me? Did you perform ablution? He said: God Almighty said: O Moses, perform ablution, but if you do not do so and a calamity befalls you, do not blame anyone but yourself. He said: I said: A questioner asks, and he said: Give charity, for charity saves you from seventy types of evil. He said: He spoke the truth, so he mentioned things from The sky, the demolition of the wall, the cutting of the animal, and drowning, God willing, among the number of disasters. He said: I said: And you will be saved from the Fire."
"9911","(9911) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Marthad ibn Abd Al-Yazani said: Someone who heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told me: The believer’s truth is his shadow on the Day of Judgment. Resurrection (Ahmed 233)"
"9912","(9912) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, who said: (He who succeeds has He purified himself. He said: He who submits."
"9913","(9913) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abu Madinah; A beggar asked Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and he had grapes in his hand, so he handed him a bunch of grapes, and it was as if they denied that, so he said: There is a lot of weight in this."
"9914","(9914) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Khalid bin Jafar, who said: I heard Abu Iyas narrating on the authority of Umm Al-Hasan; She was with Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when two poor people came and she said: Take them out? Umm Salamah said: This is not our command. I will give them dates again."
"9915","(9915) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, who said: It used to be said: Return the questioner, even if it is the equivalent of a head of cats."
"9916","(9916) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Muhammad, on the authority of Ya’la bin Abi Yahya, on the authority of Fatima bint Hussein, on the authority of Abiyya, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The beggar has a right, even if he comes riding a horse. (Abu Dawud 1463. Ahmad 1/201)"
"9917","(9917) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Jaad, he said: Jesus bin Maryam said: The questioner has a right, even if he comes riding a horse ringed with silver."
"9918","(9918) Malik bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, who said: If one of you comes The beggar, and he wants to pray, or he said: He wants to pray, if he is able to give alms, let him do it, for God He says: {Successful has indeed been he who purifies himself and mentions the name of his Lord and prays}, if he is able to present his prayers sincerely before Him. Let him do it."
"9919","(9919) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, he said: Abdullah said: Whoever does not pay zakat, There is no prayer for him."
"9920","(9920) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: There is no prayer except with zakat."
"9921","(9921) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, he said: Abdullah said: What is the objection? Zakat on a Muslim"
"9922","(9922) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abu Bakr said: If only they had prevented me from They gave the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, because of my struggle with them. He said, then recited: {And Muhammad is no more than a messenger. Messengers have passed away before him. If he dies or is killed, will you turn back on your heels?}"
"9923","(9923) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir; If you pay the zakat on your money, you will remove its evil from you."
"9924","(9924) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Zakaria bin Ishaq al-Makki narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Abdullah bin Safifi, on the authority of Abu Ma`abad, the client of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Muadh, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me He greeted him and said: You will come to a people from the People of the Book, so call them to witness that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God. If they obey that, then inform them that God has made five prayers obligatory for them every day and night. They obeyed that, so inform them that God has made it obligatory on them to give charity in their wealth, to be taken from their riches and returned to them. Their poor, if they obey that, then beware of the generous amounts of their wealth, and fear the call of the oppressed, for it is not Between us and Allah there is a veil. (Bukhari 2448. Abu Dawud 1579)"
"9925","(9925) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Cursed is he who prevents charity. (Tirmidhi 1119 and Abu Dawud 2069)"
"9926","(9926) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of al-Harith, on the authority of Ali; Like him"
"9927","(9927) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murā, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: The Levite of charity, meaning: one who prevents it, cursed according to the tongue of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the Day of Resurrection. (Ahmad 1/430, Ibn Hibban 3252)"
"9928","(9928) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muthanna bin Sa’id, who said: I heard Anas complain to a group of honest Bedouins about the truth, and he said: Gather them and fulfill them at their appointed time, so whatever is taken from you after that is an injustice you have wronged."
"9929","(9929) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jarir, who said: I said to my sons: O my sons, then The Truthful One has come to you, so do not conceal any of your blessings from him."
"9930","(9930) Ali bin Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: When the authenticator comes to you, He said: Give your charity, so give it, and if he accepts it, so be it and you will be blessed. If he refuses, then his guardian will turn away from you, and say: Oh God, I am I will take account of what is taken from me, and do not curse me."
"9931","(9931) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jarir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Let the one who confirms it come out from you when he comes out and is satisfied. Al-Sha’bi said: The one who transgresses in charity is the same as the one who denies it. (Tirmidhi 648. Ahmad 4/365)"
"9932","(9932) Khaled bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Thabit bin Qais narrated to us, on the authority of Kharijiyah bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jabir. Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There will come to you a hateful group. They come to you, welcome them, and let them be alone with you as they wish. If they do justice, it is for themselves, and if they are unjust, it is for them. And please them, for the completeness of your zakat is their satisfaction, and they will supplicate for you."
"9933","(9933) Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of al-Dahhak, who said: Whenever Omar ibn al-Khattab appeared on Money that was not included in the charity, khamsah."
"9934","(9934) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Ibn Abi Aroub told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Raziq, that he heard Al-Hasan, he said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever pays the zakat on his wealth has fulfilled the duty owed to him, and whoever increases it is better. No (Abu Dawud 130)"
"9935","(9935) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Whoever pays the zakat on his wealth There is no blame on him if he does not give charity. (Bukhari 1454; Abd al-Razzaq 7085)"
"9936","(9936) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When he reaches The money is two hundred dirhams, so it contains five dirhams."
"9937","(9937) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: Omar wrote to Abu Musa: Take from those who passed. From every two hundred dirhams, Muslim merchants get five dirhams."
"9938","(9938) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Jabir al-Hadha’, and he was a slave of the Banu Majashi’, he said : I said to Ibn Umar: Is there any zakat due on the servant? He said: Is he a Muslim? I said: Yes, he said: He must pay five dirhams for every two hundred dirhams."
"9939","(9939) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah; He said: It is permissible for him to pay zakat from the day he acquired two hundred dirhams, then one year will be due."
"9940","(9940) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: For every two hundred dirhams, five dirhams."
"9941","(9941) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who narrated it, saying: If it reaches five uqs, then in it is five. Dirhams, and for every forty dirhams there is one dirham."
"9942","(9942) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Hujair told me, on the authority of Tawus; He used to say: In two hundred dirhams, five dirhams."
"9943","(9943) Hammad bin Masadhi told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If it is two hundred dirhams, then in it are five. drama"
"9944","(9944) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr; Omar bin Abdul Aziz said: In the minerals out of every two hundred five."
"9945","(9945) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If it reaches two hundred, then in it are five dirhams."
"9946","(9946) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not be Zakat is payable on dirhams until they reach five uwaqs."
"9947","(9947) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim ibn Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: If not It is yours only for ninety-nine and one hundred, and there is no zakat on it."
"9948","(9948) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim ibn Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: There is nothing less Of two hundred dirhams zakat."
"9949","(9949) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He said: Everything less than two hundred is a Nafiqa."
"9950","(9950) Abdul Rahim bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya bin Amara; That his father Yahya bin Amara told him that he heard Abu Sa`id al-Khudri say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: There is no zakat on anything less than five uquqs, and it was valued at two hundred dirhams. (Bukhari 1447, Muslim 674)"
"9951","(9951) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He said: There is no zakat on anything less than five uwaqs of silver."
"9952","(9952) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He said: There is nothing wrong with hanging. He said: Hanging means property that does not amount to two hundred dirhams."
"9953","(9953) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is nothing in less than two hundred dirhams. (Daraqutni 93)"
"9954","(9954) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said hello and said: There is nothing less than two hundred dirhams. (Tirmidhi 620, Abu Dawud 1566)"
"9955","(9955) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Ammar bin Ruzaiq narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; Likewise, he said: Nothing is less than two hundred dirhams."
"9956","(9956) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: He did not see anything in what exceeded two hundred. Until he reaches forty."
"9957","(9957) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: Omar wrote to Abu Musa: He did not add anything more to me. Two hundred dirhams, for every forty dirhams there is a dirham."
"9958","(9958) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is nothing more than two hundred, even It is forty dirhams."
"9959","(9959) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Zayd, on the authority of Wasil the client of Abu Uyaynah, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: There is nothing more than two hundred dirhams, until it reaches forty dirhams."
"9960","(9960) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Until it reaches forty-odd dirhams. The two hundred is then six dirhams, then nothing until you reach two hundred and eighty dirhams, which is seven. Dirhams, then the same."
"9961","(9961) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim ibn Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: There is nothing less From two hundred dirhams is something, and whatever is more is to be reckoned with."
"9962","(9962) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Jabir al-Hadha’, and he was a slave of Banu Mujasha’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: Whatever exceeds two hundred, then it will be based on reckoning."
"9963","(9963) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whatever exceeds two hundred will be brought to account."
"9964","(9964) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Whatever is increased is for reckoning."
"9965","(9965) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, he said: He did not increase So by calculation."
"9966","(9966) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim ibn Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: There is nothing less Of twenty dinars there is something, and of twenty dinars there is half a dinar, and of forty dinars there is a dinar, and whatever is more is to be paid upon account."
"9967","(9967) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamiya ibn Marthad, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: In twenty mithqals, half a mithqal. And in forty mithqals there is one mithqal."
"9968","(9968) Hammad bin Masadi narrated to us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: In forty dinars is one dinar, and in Twenty dinars, half a dinar."
"9969","(9969) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: In twenty dinars, half a dinar."
"9970","(9970) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is not less than twenty mithqals. One thing, and in twenty there is half a mithqal, and in forty mithqals there is a mithqal."
"9971","(9971) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Raziq, the client of Banu Fazaria; Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to him when he was appointed caliph: Take from among the Muslim merchants who passed you what they are managing. Their money, for every forty dinars, whatever decreases, then calculate the decrease until it reaches twenty. If it decreases by one-third A dinar and leave it, do not take anything from it, and write for them a release of what you take from them for a similar amount within a year. And take from those of the non-Muslims who pass by you, from every twenty A dinar is a dinar, and whatever decreases, he calculates what has decreased until it reaches ten dinars. If it decreases by a third of a dinar, he leaves it, no. Take something from them, and write for them a disavowal of something similar to it in the same way as what you take from them."
"9972","(9972) Muhammad bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is not in anything less than forty mithqals of gold. He spoke the truth"
"9973","(9973) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyya told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam; He did not consider zakat on twenty dinars, until they were twenty mithqals, in which case it would contain half a mithqal."
"9974","(9974) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; He said: Abdullah’s wife had a ring containing twenty mithqals, so he ordered her to take out five dirhams from it."
"9975","(9975) Hammad bin Masadi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: In twenty dinars, half a dinar, and in forty. A dinar is a dinar."
"9976","(9976) Hammad bin Masadi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is nothing less than forty dinars."
"9977","(9977) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ said: There should be no charity in wealth until it reaches Twenty dinars. If it reaches twenty dinars, then half a dinar is added to it, and for every four dinars, the money increases. A dirham, until it reaches forty dinars, and for every forty dinars there is a dinar, and for every twenty-four dinars there is half a dinar. dinar and dirham."
"9978","(9978) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ubad, who said: I asked Abraham about a man who had a hundred dirhams and ten dirhams. dinars? He said: He pays zakat on the hundred dirhams, two and a half dirhams, and on the dinars, a quarter of a dinar. He said: I asked Al-Sha’abi, and he said: The most is accepted as the least. Or he said: The less is more than the more, so if the amount of zakat is due, then zakat is due."
"9979","(9979) Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Ubaid, who said: I said to Makhul: O Abu Abdullah, I have A sword containing fifty and a hundred dirhams, so pay zakat on it. He said: Add to it whatever gold you have. And silver. If it reaches two hundred dirhams of gold and silver, then you must pay zakat on it."
"9980","(9980) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: If she had Thirty dinars and a hundred dirhams, which he had to pay as charity, and he saw the dirhams and dinars as the same as all of them."
"9981","(9981) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Omar; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote the Book of Charity and connected it to his sword, or he said: with his will, and he did not He took it out until it was killed, and when it was killed, Abu Bakr worked with it until it died, then Umar worked with it, and it was: in five of There are two sheep in camels, and in ten there are two sheep, and in fifteen there are three sheep, and in twenty-five there are four sheep, and in twenty-five there are Bint Makhad is up to thirty-five, and if it increases, then its due is up to Bint Labun, up to forty-five, and if it increases, then its entitlement is up to Sixty, then if it is increased, then Jada’iah is up to seventy-five, and if it is increased, then Binta Labun is ninety, and if it is increased, then two fahaqatan is up to Twenty and a hundred, but if it is more than twenty and a hundred, then for every fifty there is a right, and for every forty there is a Bint Labun, no. It combines what is separate, and does not differentiate between a community, and if there are two mixtures, they come together as one. (Tirmidhi 621, Abu Dawud 1562)"
"9982","(9982) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, and Ziyad bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: In Twenty-five camels from Bint Makhad."
"9983","(9983) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: In five camels there is a sheep. Up to nine, and if it increases by one, then there are two sheep in it, up to fourteen, and if it increases by one, then there are three sheep in it, up to fourteen. Nineteen, if it increases one, it has four to twenty-four, if it increases one, it has five sheep. If it increases by one, then it includes Bint Makhad, or a male Ibn Labun, one year older than her, up to thirty-five. One, then it has the right of Bint Labun up to forty-five, and if it increases one, then it has the right of Tarooqih of the stallion up to sixty. If it increases by one, then it has a Jadbi’ah up to seventy-five, and if it increases by one, then it has a Bint Labun up to ninety. If it exceeds one, then it has two heques, up to twenty and a hundred. If there are a lot of camels, then every fifty camels have a right, and no It brings together the divided, but does not differentiate between the two communities."
"9984","(9984) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: It was found in Omar’s will: in five. And twenty camels from Bint Makhad."
"9985","(9985) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi (H) and on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim. They said: There are twenty-five daughters. labor"
"9986","(9986) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Baz ibn Hakim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: For every free-riding camel there are forty bint Labun. No camel is separated from its account. Whoever gives it to a tenant will have it. His reward is one of the gifts of our Lord, none of which is permissible for the family of Muhammad. (Abu Dawud 1569. Ahmad 5/4)"
"9987","(9987) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Umar said: If it increases For camels, there is a camel for every fifty, and a camel for every forty."
"9988","(9988) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: In every twenty-five there is a Bint Makhad."
"9989","(9989) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: It was in the book that Omar bin Abd wrote Al-Aziz, when He sent them to sacrifice camels: When they reach the age of twenty-five, then there is Bint Makhad in them, and if they are older, then Ibn Labun. male"
"9990","(9990) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Hammad, who said: In the twenty-five of Bint Makhad."
"9991","(9991) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to Manna is to be taken from camels, from every fifth sheep, from every ten sheep there are two sheep, from every fifteen sheep there are thirteen sheep, and from Twenty is four sheikhs, and from twenty-five is five sheikhs, so if it is added by one, it has a bint makhad to five. And thirty. If the camels do not find Bint Makhad, then Bint Labun is a male. If there is more than one, then Bint Labun, up to five. And forty, if it is increased by one, then it has a right up to sixty, and if it is increased by one, then it has a jud’ah, up to seventy-five. If it increases by one, then it has two bint Labun, up to ninety. If it increases by one, then it has two hiqqahs, up to one hundred and twenty. If there are many camels, then for every fifty there is a camel, and for every forty there is a bint Labun, and there is no distinction between a group, nor It is combined between two parts, and no he-goat, or an old woman, or a one-married woman is to be taken in charity. Al-Ajlah said: So I said to Al-Shaabi: What is meant by his saying: He does not unite what is separate, and he does not separate between a group? He said: A man has the sheep, but he does not disperse them, so that no zakat is taken from them, nor brings together divided people. They have sheep on which zakat is not required, so they are not gathered together and zakat is taken from them."
"9992","(9992) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, who said: If not There are only four animals, and there is no zakat in them."
"9993","(9993) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali and Abdullah, that they said: There is no Less than five camels are zakat."
"9994","(9994) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: We have been informed that Salem bin Abdullah used to say: We have the letter of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab about the charity of camels, but no one asked us about it, until Omar Ibn Abdul-Aziz came to us. So We sent it to him, and it was in the letter that Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote when he sent them that they believed: There is a zakat on camels until they reach the age of five."
"9995","(9995) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya bin Amara, on the authority of his father On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no zakat in less than a fifth of an animal."
"9996","(9996) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: There is nothing in less than five dhuds."
"9997","(9997) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: There is no zakat on anything less than five times a day. (Ahmad 2/92, Bazzar 888)"
"9998","(9998) Ali bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no zakat in less than one-fifth of an animal. (Ahmad 2/403, Tahawi 35)"
"9999","(9999) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Omar; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wrote the book of charity, and he tied it to his sword, or he said: by his will, but he did not bring it out. Until he was arrested, Abu Bakr worked on it until he died, then Omar worked on it until he died, and it was: in camels if they exceed Twenty and a hundred, so in every fifty there is a share, and in every forty there is a son of Labun."
"10000","(10,000) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: If there are many camels, then Every fifty is a right."
"10001","(10001) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to Yemen: If there are many camels, then in every fifty there is a camel, and in every forty there is a Bint Labun."
"10002","(10002) Abdul bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: It was found in Omar’s will that he was more than twenty. And a hundred, so in every forty there is a Bint Labun, and in every fifty there is a hiqqah."
"10003","(10003) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If there are a lot of camels, then every fifty has a due share."
"10004","(10004) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: We were informed that Salim used to say: We have The letter of Omar about the charity of camels and sheep, until the letter of Omar bin Abdulaziz was presented to us, and it was in the book that was written Omar bin Abdulaziz, when they were sent, they believed: If it exceeds one hundred and twenty, then in every fifty there is a right, and in every Forty bint Labun."
"10005","(10005) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: If it is more than twenty and a hundred, the obligatory prayer is accepted with it."
"10006","(10006) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Like him."
"10007","(10007) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of al-Sanabihi al-Ahmasi, He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a beautiful camel riding on the camels of al-Sadaqah, and he said: What is this? The owner of the truth said: I took it back with two camels, and he said: So yes, then. (Ahmad 4/349, Tabarani 7417)"
"10008","(10008) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Hilal Ibn Khabbab, on the authority of Misra Abu Salih, he said: Suwayd Ibn Ghafla narrated to us, He said: The authenticity of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us, so I came to him and sat next to him, and I heard him say: In my covenant not It was taken from a milk-breastfeeding woman, and it is not combined between separate ones, nor is it differentiated between combined ones. He said: A man brought him a camel as a pile of sheep. He refused to take it. (Abu Dawud 1573. Tabarani 6473)"
"10009","(10009) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent a believer, and he said: Do not take anything from the regrets of people’s souls, but take what is near, and The shame. (Byd 102)"
"10010","(10010) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a beautiful camel in the The camel of charity, and he said: What is the matter with this camel? Then the one who gave the charity said: O Messenger of God, I knew your need for a zihar, so I satisfied it with two camels of charity."
"10011","(10011) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya, on the authority of Al-Qasim; Omar passed by one of the sadaqah sheep, and he saw among them a sheep with an udder, and he said: What is this? They said: From the sheep of charity. He said: This is what he gave to its people while they were obedient. Do not tempt people, do not take people’s advice. They abstained from food."
"10012","(10012) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdullah bin Sayfi, on the authority of Abu Ma’bad On the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Muadh, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Beware of the generous amounts of their wealth, when he was sent to Yemen."
"10013","(10013) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said hello. He said: There are thirty cows you sell, or you sell, and there are forty old ones. (Tirmidhi 622. Ahmad 1/411)"
"10014","(10014) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent May the peace and blessings of God be upon him and his family, Muadh was sent to Yemen. He commanded him to take from every thirty cows a ta’ba’, or a ta’ba’a, and from every Forty elderly people, and from every dreamer a dinar, or a clean saddlebag. (Abu Dawud 1571)"
"10015","(10015) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to Yemen: to be taken from the cows of thirty taba'a, or taba'a'a, and in every forty there is a masannah."
"10016","(10016) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim and Abu Wa’il, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent Mu’adh To Yemen, and ordered him to take some cows from every thirty tabi`a or tabi`a, and from forty musnnah, and from Every dreamer receives a dinar, or his equivalent of a sanctuary. (Abu Dawud 1570, An-Nasa’i 2232)"
"10017","(10017) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, He said: If she reaches thirty, then there is a sale in her, or a yearly sale, and if she reaches forty, then in her is a Masnah, two. Onwards."
"10018","(10018) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: I was informed that Mu’adh said: In thirty taba’a. And forty cows."
"10019","(10019) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There are thirty cows to be sold, or A jud'ah, or a jud'ah, and for forty musannahs."
"10020","(10020) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Shehr, he said: In the sale of cows, in every thirty you sell, And in every forty women."
